INSERT INTO `reading_articles` VALUES (35,'en','Why Your Library Is the Most Important Place in Town','In an age where digital devices dominate our lives, it is easy to overlook the physical spaces that once served as the cornerstones of our communities. The public library is one such space. Far from being a relic of the past, the library remains a vital institution that serves the public in ways that extend well beyond lending books. Libraries provide access to information, technology, and educational resources for people of all ages and backgrounds. They bridge the digital divide by offering free internet access and computer training to those who cannot afford these services at home. For job seekers, libraries offer career counseling, resume workshops, and access to online job portals. For immigrants, they provide language classes and citizenship resources. Libraries also serve as community gathering places where people from diverse backgrounds can come together for book clubs, cultural events, and public forums. In an increasingly polarized society, libraries remain one of the few places where individuals of different political views, economic statuses, and cultural backgrounds can interact on equal footing. Studies have shown that communities with strong public libraries have higher levels of civic engagement and social cohesion. Moreover, libraries play a crucial role in early childhood development through story times, summer reading programs, and parent education workshops. These programs help narrow the achievement gap between children from different socioeconomic backgrounds. Despite the proliferation of e-books and online resources, physical library visits have remained remarkably stable in many communities, suggesting that the library functions as more than just a book repository. It is a social infrastructure that strengthens the fabric of our communities in ways both visible and invisible.',450,NULL,NULL,'专业人士','society,culture,education','2026-07-02 12:31:45',5,'[{\"word\": \"cornerstone\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkɔːrnərstoʊn/\", \"definition\": \"基石；基础\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"vital\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈvaɪtl/\", \"definition\": \"至关重要的；生机勃勃的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"bridge\", \"phonetic\": \"/brɪdʒ/\", \"definition\": \"弥合（差距）；架桥\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"polarized\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈpoʊləraɪzd/\", \"definition\": \"两极分化的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"civic engagement\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈsɪvɪk ɪnˈɡeɪdʒmənt/\", \"definition\": \"公民参与\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}, {\"word\": \"cohesion\", \"phonetic\": \"/koʊˈhiːʒn/\", \"definition\": \"凝聚力；团结\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"proliferation\", \"phonetic\": \"/prəˌlɪfəˈreɪʃn/\", \"definition\": \"激增；扩散\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"infrastructure\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃər/\", \"definition\": \"基础设施\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Libraries are outdated because of digital devices.\", \"B. Libraries are still important community institutions that provide many services beyond lending books.\", \"C. Libraries only help job seekers and immigrants.\", \"D. Libraries are no longer visited by people due to e-books.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出数字设备主导生活，但图书馆并非过时，而是仍然重要的机构，提供信息、技术、教育资源等多项服务，并促进社区凝聚力。选项B概括了主旨，其他选项与原文相反或片面。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Free housing assistance.\", \"B. Career counseling and resume workshops.\", \"C. Free medical checkups.\", \"D. Legal advice for small businesses.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, which of the following is a service libraries provide for job seekers?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到“For job seekers, libraries offer career counseling, resume workshops, and access to online job portals.” 选项B与此一致，其他选项未在文中提及。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. People prefer e-books over physical books.\", \"B. Libraries are only used for borrowing books.\", \"C. Libraries serve a social and community function beyond just providing books.\", \"D. The number of library visitors is decreasing rapidly.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred from the fact that \'physical library visits have remained remarkably stable\' despite e-books and online resources?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章提到尽管电子书和在线资源普及，实体图书馆访问量仍保持稳定，并指出图书馆是“social infrastructure that strengthens the fabric of our communities”，暗示其社会功能远超借书。选项C符合推理，其他选项与原文信息矛盾。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Libraries are outdated because of digital devices.\", \"B. Libraries are still important community institutions that provide many services beyond lending books.\", \"C. Libraries only help job seekers and immigrants.\", \"D. Libraries are no longer visited by people due to e-books.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出数字设备主导生活，但图书馆并非过时，而是仍然重要的机构，提供信息、技术、教育资源等多项服务，并促进社区凝聚力。选项B概括了主旨，其他选项与原文相反或片面。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Libraries are outdated because of digital devices.\", \"B. Libraries are still important community institutions that provide many services beyond lending books.\", \"C. Libraries only help job seekers and immigrants.\", \"D. Libraries are no longer visited by people due to e-books.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出数字设备主导生活，但图书馆并非过时，而是仍然重要的机构，提供信息、技术、教育资源等多项服务，并促进社区凝聚力。选项B概括了主旨，其他选项与原文相反或片面。\"}]'),(36,'en','School Absences and Academic Achievement','Nationally, one in six children miss 15 or more days of school in a year, a benchmark that researchers use to define chronic absenteeism. The problem has drawn the attention of policymakers at the highest levels. The U.S. Secretary of Education recently issued an open letter calling on states and school districts to take action, noting that student achievement cannot improve if children are not in school. But new research suggests that the picture is more complex than it first appears. The authors of a recent study make a crucial distinction between excused and unexcused absences. They find that excused absences, typically for illness or family emergencies, have little impact on children\'s long-term academic outcomes. Unexcused absences, on the other hand, are a different story altogether. These absences reflect the broader challenges that children face outside of school, including poverty, housing instability, and lack of access to healthcare. The researchers argue that education policies have long been built on an assumption: if schools do their job well, they can overcome the effects of poverty and inequality. But the reality is that schools alone cannot solve problems that originate in the community. The most effective interventions are not those that punish parents for their children\'s absences, but those that provide resources to struggling families. This might include connecting families with social services, providing transportation assistance, or offering school-based health clinics.',380,NULL,NULL,'CET6','education,society','2026-07-02 12:31:58',4,'[{\"word\": \"chronic absenteeism\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkrɒnɪk ˌæbsənˈtiːɪzəm/\", \"definition\": \"长期缺勤\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"policymaker\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈpɒlɪsiˌmeɪkər/\", \"definition\": \"政策制定者\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"distinction\", \"phonetic\": \"/dɪˈstɪŋkʃən/\", \"definition\": \"区分；差别\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"excused absence\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪkˈskjuːzd ˈæbsəns/\", \"definition\": \"请假缺勤\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"unexcused absence\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌʌnɪkˈskjuːzd ˈæbsəns/\", \"definition\": \"无故缺勤\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"instability\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌɪnstəˈbɪləti/\", \"definition\": \"不稳定\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"intervention\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌɪntərˈvenʃən/\", \"definition\": \"干预；介入\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"inequality\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌɪnɪˈkwɒləti/\", \"definition\": \"不平等\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Chronic absenteeism is a serious problem that can be solved by punishing parents.\", \"B. Unexcused absences are more harmful than excused absences, and schools alone cannot solve the root causes.\", \"C. The U.S. Secretary of Education believes that student achievement can improve even if children miss school.\", \"D. Excused absences have a greater impact on long-term academic outcomes than unexcused absences.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主旨是区分了因病因事请假（excused absences）和无故缺勤（unexcused absences），指出后者危害更大，且根源在于社区问题（如贫困、住房不稳定），学校无法独自解决，因此最有效的干预是提供资源而非惩罚。选项B准确概括了这一核心观点。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. One in ten\", \"B. One in six\", \"C. One in four\", \"D. One in eight\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what percentage of children nationally miss 15 or more days of school per year?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章第一句明确指出“Nationally, one in six children miss 15 or more days of school in a year”，即六分之一的孩子每年缺课15天或以上。选项B与此一致。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. They believe that schools can overcome the effects of poverty if they perform well.\", \"B. They think that punishing parents is the most effective way to reduce absenteeism.\", \"C. They suggest that policies should focus on providing community resources rather than blaming families.\", \"D. They argue that excused absences are the main cause of long-term academic failure.\"], \"question\": \"Based on the passage, which of the following can be inferred about the researchers\' view on education policies?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：推理题。文章指出“the most effective interventions are not those that punish parents... but those that provide resources to struggling families”，并举例包括连接社会服务、交通援助、学校健康诊所等。由此可推断，研究者认为政策应聚焦于提供社区资源而非惩罚家庭。选项C符合这一推理。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Chronic absenteeism is a serious problem that can be solved by punishing parents.\", \"B. Unexcused absences are more harmful than excused absences, and schools alone cannot solve the root causes.\", \"C. The U.S. Secretary of Education believes that student achievement can improve even if children miss school.\", \"D. Excused absences have a greater impact on long-term academic outcomes than unexcused absences.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主旨是区分了因病因事请假（excused absences）和无故缺勤（unexcused absences），指出后者危害更大，且根源在于社区问题（如贫困、住房不稳定），学校无法独自解决，因此最有效的干预是提供资源而非惩罚。选项B准确概括了这一核心观点。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Chronic absenteeism is a serious problem that can be solved by punishing parents.\", \"B. Unexcused absences are more harmful than excused absences, and schools alone cannot solve the root causes.\", \"C. The U.S. Secretary of Education believes that student achievement can improve even if children miss school.\", \"D. Excused absences have a greater impact on long-term academic outcomes than unexcused absences.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主旨是区分了因病因事请假（excused absences）和无故缺勤（unexcused absences），指出后者危害更大，且根源在于社区问题（如贫困、住房不稳定），学校无法独自解决，因此最有效的干预是提供资源而非惩罚。选项B准确概括了这一核心观点。\"}]'),(37,'en','The Limits of \'Follow Your Passion\'','After earning a bachelor\'s degree, I was determined to do what I love. I had been told throughout my life that the key to a fulfilling career was to follow my passion. For nearly a decade, I gave this advice to others as well. But over time, through my own research and experience, I came to question the wisdom of the passion principle. The advice to follow your passion sounds empowering. It suggests that career success is a matter of personal choice and self-discovery. But its popularity conceals a darker reality. For one thing, not all passions are equally valued by the labor market. A passion for software engineering is likely to lead to a stable, well-paying career, while a passion for poetry or social justice is far less marketable. More importantly, the ability to turn a passion into a livelihood depends heavily on access to resources that are unequally distributed: financial support from family, social networks, and educational opportunities. When we tell everyone to follow their passion, we ignore these structural inequalities. The result is that those from privileged backgrounds are more likely to succeed in pursuing their passions, while those from disadvantaged backgrounds may blame themselves when they cannot. The passion principle, in effect, legitimizes inequality by making career outcomes seem like a matter of individual choice rather than structural constraint. Furthermore, the passion principle can be exploited by employers. Workers who are passionate about their jobs are often expected to tolerate lower pay, longer hours, and worse working conditions precisely because they love what they do.',390,NULL,NULL,'CET6','career,society,economy','2026-07-02 12:32:11',4,'[{\"word\": \"fulfilling\", \"phonetic\": \"/fʊlˈfɪlɪŋ/\", \"definition\": \"令人满足的；有成就感的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"conceals\", \"phonetic\": \"/kənˈsiːlz/\", \"definition\": \"隐藏；掩盖\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"marketable\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈmɑːrkɪtəbl/\", \"definition\": \"有市场价值的；畅销的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"livelihood\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈlaɪvlihʊd/\", \"definition\": \"生计；谋生手段\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"unequally\", \"phonetic\": \"/ʌnˈiːkwəli/\", \"definition\": \"不平等地；不均衡地\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adverb\"}, {\"word\": \"structural\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈstrʌktʃərəl/\", \"definition\": \"结构性的；结构上的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"privileged\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒd/\", \"definition\": \"有特权的；享有优惠的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"exploited\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪkˈsplɔɪtɪd/\", \"definition\": \"被利用的；被剥削的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb (past participle)\"}]','[{\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Following your passion always leads to a fulfilling career.\", \"B. The passion principle is a simple and effective career advice.\", \"C. The passion principle ignores structural inequalities and can be exploited by employers.\", \"D. People should only pursue passions that are marketable.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要批判了‘追随激情’这一职业建议，指出它忽视了结构性不平等（如资源分配不均）并可能被雇主利用（如要求低薪长时工作）。选项C准确概括了主旨。A与作者观点相反；B与作者质疑的态度矛盾；D过于片面，作者并未要求只追求有市场价值的激情。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. It guarantees high income for all passionate workers.\", \"B. It assumes everyone has equal access to resources to pursue their passion.\", \"C. It encourages people to work in fields they dislike.\", \"D. It is only applicable to creative professions like poetry.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, which of the following is a reason why the passion principle can be problematic?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：细节题。文中明确指出‘the ability to turn a passion into a livelihood depends heavily on access to resources that are unequally distributed’，即该原则假设人人拥有平等资源，但实际并非如此。选项B正确。A与文中‘not all passions are equally valued by the labor market’矛盾；C与‘follow your passion’本意相反；D文中未提及仅适用于创意行业。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. The author believes it is the best advice for career success.\", \"B. The author thinks it is a harmless and neutral suggestion.\", \"C. The author considers it a misleading idea that reinforces social inequality.\", \"D. The author supports it as long as one chooses a marketable passion.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author\'s view on the phrase \'follow your passion\'?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：推断题。作者指出该建议‘legitimizes inequality by making career outcomes seem like a matter of individual choice’，并批评其被雇主利用，可见作者认为它具有误导性且加剧不平等。选项C正确。A与作者质疑的态度相反；B与‘conceals a darker reality’矛盾；D文中未提及作者支持该建议。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Following your passion always leads to a fulfilling career.\", \"B. The passion principle is a simple and effective career advice.\", \"C. The passion principle ignores structural inequalities and can be exploited by employers.\", \"D. People should only pursue passions that are marketable.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要批判了‘追随激情’这一职业建议，指出它忽视了结构性不平等（如资源分配不均）并可能被雇主利用（如要求低薪长时工作）。选项C准确概括了主旨。A与作者观点相反；B与作者质疑的态度矛盾；D过于片面，作者并未要求只追求有市场价值的激情。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Following your passion always leads to a fulfilling career.\", \"B. The passion principle is a simple and effective career advice.\", \"C. The passion principle ignores structural inequalities and can be exploited by employers.\", \"D. People should only pursue passions that are marketable.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要批判了‘追随激情’这一职业建议，指出它忽视了结构性不平等（如资源分配不均）并可能被雇主利用（如要求低薪长时工作）。选项C准确概括了主旨。A与作者观点相反；B与作者质疑的态度矛盾；D过于片面，作者并未要求只追求有市场价值的激情。\"}]'),(38,'en','Tardigrades: Earth\'s Toughest Creatures','No beast on Earth is tougher than the tiny tardigrade. These microscopic creatures, also known as water bears, can survive conditions that would kill almost any other living thing. They have been blasted into space, subjected to intense radiation, frozen to near absolute zero, and boiled to over 150 degrees Celsius. Each time, they have survived. The secret to their resilience lies in their remarkable adaptations. When faced with extreme environmental conditions, tardigrades can enter a state called cryptobiosis, in which they essentially shut down their metabolism and expel almost all the water from their bodies, curling up into a tiny, indestructible ball known as a tun. In this state, they can withstand the rigors of space, the pressure of the deepest ocean trenches, and radiation levels that would seem catastrophic to other organisms. Scientists have been studying these creatures intensively in recent years because their unique biology could have applications from preserving vaccines without refrigeration to protecting human cells from radiation damage. Despite their seemingly simple appearance, tardigrades have an extraordinarily complex genetic makeup, with a significant portion of their DNA having been acquired from other organisms through horizontal gene transfer. Understanding how tardigrades evolved their extreme survival capabilities may help us develop new technologies for everything from space travel to medicine.',320,NULL,NULL,'CET6','science,biology','2026-07-02 12:32:25',4,'[{\"word\": \"tardigrade\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈtɑːrdɪɡreɪd/\", \"definition\": \"缓步动物（俗称水熊虫）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"resilience\", \"phonetic\": \"/rɪˈzɪliəns/\", \"definition\": \"恢复力；适应力\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"cryptobiosis\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkrɪptoʊbaɪˈoʊsɪs/\", \"definition\": \"隐生现象（代谢停止的极端休眠状态）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"metabolism\", \"phonetic\": \"/məˈtæbəlɪzəm/\", \"definition\": \"新陈代谢\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"catastrophic\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkætəˈstrɑːfɪk/\", \"definition\": \"灾难性的；毁灭性的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"horizontal gene transfer\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌhɔːrɪˈzɒntl dʒiːn trænsˈfɜːr/\", \"definition\": \"水平基因转移\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}, {\"word\": \"genetic makeup\", \"phonetic\": \"/dʒəˈnetɪk ˈmeɪkʌp/\", \"definition\": \"遗传构成；基因组成\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tardigrades are the most dangerous creatures on Earth.\", \"B. Tardigrades are tiny but extremely resilient due to unique adaptations.\", \"C. Scientists have fully decoded the tardigrade genome.\", \"D. Tardigrades can only survive in space.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要介绍了缓步动物（水熊虫）体型微小但生命力极强，核心在于其独特的适应能力（如隐生状态），因此B项正确。A项‘最危险’无依据；C项‘完全解码’未提及；D项‘只能在太空生存’与文中多种极端环境不符。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. It becomes larger and more active.\", \"B. It reproduces rapidly.\", \"C. It expels water and curls into a tun.\", \"D. It develops a hard outer shell.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what happens when a tardigrade enters cryptobiosis?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：细节题。文中明确描述‘expel almost all the water from their bodies, curling up into a tiny, indestructible ball known as a tun’，因此C项正确。A、B、D均与原文不符。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tardigrades could be used as food for astronauts.\", \"B. Their survival mechanisms might help preserve medicines without cooling.\", \"C. Scientists plan to create giant tardigrades for space travel.\", \"D. Tardigrade DNA is too simple to be useful.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the potential applications of tardigrade research?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：推理题。文中提到‘their unique biology could have applications from preserving vaccines without refrigeration’，因此可推断其生存机制可能帮助无需冷藏保存药物，B项正确。A项‘作为食物’、C项‘制造巨型水熊虫’、D项‘DNA太简单’均与原文信息矛盾。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tardigrades are the most dangerous creatures on Earth.\", \"B. Tardigrades are tiny but extremely resilient due to unique adaptations.\", \"C. Scientists have fully decoded the tardigrade genome.\", \"D. Tardigrades can only survive in space.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要介绍了缓步动物（水熊虫）体型微小但生命力极强，核心在于其独特的适应能力（如隐生状态），因此B项正确。A项‘最危险’无依据；C项‘完全解码’未提及；D项‘只能在太空生存’与文中多种极端环境不符。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tardigrades are the most dangerous creatures on Earth.\", \"B. Tardigrades are tiny but extremely resilient due to unique adaptations.\", \"C. Scientists have fully decoded the tardigrade genome.\", \"D. Tardigrades can only survive in space.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要介绍了缓步动物（水熊虫）体型微小但生命力极强，核心在于其独特的适应能力（如隐生状态），因此B项正确。A项‘最危险’无依据；C项‘完全解码’未提及；D项‘只能在太空生存’与文中多种极端环境不符。\"}]'),(39,'en','Career Anxiety and Status Anxiety','Why are we so worried about our careers? Partly it is to do with money, but there is a psychological aspect to our fears as well. Beneath the surface of career anxiety often lies a more fundamental worry: status anxiety. We live in a society that judges people largely by what they do for a living. When we meet someone new, one of the first questions we ask is, \'What do you do?\' The answer we receive immediately colors our perception of that person. A surgeon commands more respect than a sanitation worker, even though both perform essential functions. This is not simply snobbery. The desire for status is deeply rooted in human psychology. Throughout history, high social status has been associated with better access to resources, greater reproductive opportunities, and increased safety. But in modern society, our status is largely determined by our occupation, making career choice a matter of profound psychological importance. The problem is that there are not enough high-status, well-paying jobs to go around. And so career anxiety is as much about our place in the social hierarchy as it is about paychecks. The author suggests that we would do well to be more skeptical of the status hierarchies that govern our working lives, and to be kinder to and more curious about the people we encounter, regardless of what they do for a living.',370,NULL,NULL,'CET6','psychology,career,society','2026-07-02 12:32:39',4,'[{\"word\": \"anxiety\", \"phonetic\": \"/æŋˈzaɪəti/\", \"definition\": \"焦虑；忧虑\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"status\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈsteɪtəs/\", \"definition\": \"地位；身份\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"perception\", \"phonetic\": \"/pərˈsepʃn/\", \"definition\": \"看法；感知\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"snobbery\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈsnɒbəri/\", \"definition\": \"势利；媚上欺下\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"hierarchy\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈhaɪərɑːrki/\", \"definition\": \"等级制度；层级\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"profound\", \"phonetic\": \"/prəˈfaʊnd/\", \"definition\": \"深刻的；极大的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"skeptical\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈskeptɪkl/\", \"definition\": \"怀疑的；持怀疑态度的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"encounter\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪnˈkaʊntər/\", \"definition\": \"遇到；邂逅\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Career anxiety is primarily caused by financial concerns.\", \"B. Status anxiety, rooted in human psychology and social judgment, is a key driver of career worry.\", \"C. High-status jobs like surgeons are more important than jobs like sanitation workers.\", \"D. Modern society has eliminated the link between occupation and social status.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出职业焦虑部分源于金钱，但更根本的是‘地位焦虑’（status anxiety）。随后解释了社会以职业评判人、地位与心理需求相关，并指出职业焦虑关乎社会层级。选项B概括了这一核心观点。A过于片面；C与原文‘both perform essential functions’矛盾；D与原文‘status is largely determined by our occupation’相反。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. To find out how much money the person earns.\", \"B. To determine the person\'s social status and form an impression.\", \"C. To check if the person has a high-status job like a surgeon.\", \"D. To start a conversation about career advice.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, why do people ask \'What do you do?\' when meeting someone new?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文明确说‘The answer we receive immediately colors our perception of that person’，即答案会立刻影响我们对这个人的看法。结合前文‘judges people largely by what they do for a living’，可知提问是为了判断对方的社会地位并形成印象。A（金钱）是部分原因但非直接目的；C过于具体；D未提及。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. The author believes status hierarchies are fair and necessary.\", \"B. The author thinks people should ignore status and focus only on money.\", \"C. The author suggests we should question status hierarchies and treat people equally regardless of occupation.\", \"D. The author argues that status anxiety is a modern problem with no historical roots.\"], \"question\": \"Based on the passage, what can be inferred about the author\'s view on status hierarchies?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章结尾作者建议‘be more skeptical of the status hierarchies’以及‘be kinder to and more curious about the people... regardless of what they do’，这暗示作者认为我们应该质疑地位等级，并平等对待所有人。A与‘skeptical’矛盾；B‘focus only on money’未提及；D与‘Throughout history...’的历史根源描述相反。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Career anxiety is primarily caused by financial concerns.\", \"B. Status anxiety, rooted in human psychology and social judgment, is a key driver of career worry.\", \"C. High-status jobs like surgeons are more important than jobs like sanitation workers.\", \"D. Modern society has eliminated the link between occupation and social status.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出职业焦虑部分源于金钱，但更根本的是‘地位焦虑’（status anxiety）。随后解释了社会以职业评判人、地位与心理需求相关，并指出职业焦虑关乎社会层级。选项B概括了这一核心观点。A过于片面；C与原文‘both perform essential functions’矛盾；D与原文‘status is largely determined by our occupation’相反。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Career anxiety is primarily caused by financial concerns.\", \"B. Status anxiety, rooted in human psychology and social judgment, is a key driver of career worry.\", \"C. High-status jobs like surgeons are more important than jobs like sanitation workers.\", \"D. Modern society has eliminated the link between occupation and social status.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出职业焦虑部分源于金钱，但更根本的是‘地位焦虑’（status anxiety）。随后解释了社会以职业评判人、地位与心理需求相关，并指出职业焦虑关乎社会层级。选项B概括了这一核心观点。A过于片面；C与原文‘both perform essential functions’矛盾；D与原文‘status is largely determined by our occupation’相反。\"}]'),(40,'en','The Gender Pay Gap: Progress and Stagnation','Women have historically been paid less than men, but for much of the late 20th century, the gender pay gap was shrinking rapidly. In the 1980s, the gap between men\'s and women\'s median hourly earnings closed at an impressive rate. Many economists believed that if this trend continued, full gender pay equality would be achieved by the early 21st century. But that did not happen. Since the mid-1990s, progress on closing the gender pay gap has slowed dramatically. The rate of gender wage convergence fell noticeably, and in some years, the gap even widened slightly. What explains this stagnation? Researchers point to several factors, but chief among them is the unequal burden of family responsibilities. Women continue to shoulder a disproportionate share of childcare and housework, and many step back from their careers, either temporarily or permanently, after having children. This \'child penalty\' accounts for a large portion of the remaining gender pay gap. Furthermore, occupations dominated by women, such as teaching and nursing, have historically been undervalued and underpaid relative to male-dominated professions requiring similar levels of education and skill. Closing the gender pay gap completely will require not only workplace policies that support working parents, such as paid family leave and affordable childcare, but also a broader cultural shift in how we value the work that women do.',380,NULL,NULL,'CET6','society,economy,gender','2026-07-02 12:32:52',4,'[{\"word\": \"stagnation\", \"phonetic\": \"/stæɡˈneɪʃən/\", \"definition\": \"停滞；不发展\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"convergence\", \"phonetic\": \"/kənˈvɜːrdʒəns/\", \"definition\": \"趋同；收敛\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"disproportionate\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌdɪsprəˈpɔːrʃənət/\", \"definition\": \"不成比例的；不相称的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"shoulder\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈʃoʊldər/\", \"definition\": \"承担；肩负\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"penalty\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈpenəlti/\", \"definition\": \"惩罚；不利后果\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"dominate\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈdɑːmɪneɪt/\", \"definition\": \"主导；支配\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"undervalue\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌʌndərˈvæljuː/\", \"definition\": \"低估；轻视\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"cultural shift\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkʌltʃərəl ʃɪft/\", \"definition\": \"文化转变；观念变革\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The gender pay gap has been shrinking steadily since the 1980s.\", \"B. The gender pay gap stopped shrinking in the mid-1990s due to several factors, including family responsibilities and occupational undervaluation.\", \"C. Women are paid less than men because they choose lower-paying jobs.\", \"D. The gender pay gap will disappear automatically with better workplace policies.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讨论了性别薪酬差距在20世纪80年代快速缩小，但自90年代中期以来停滞不前，并分析了主要原因（家庭责任和职业价值低估），因此选项B正确概括了主旨。选项A错误，因为90年代中期后进展放缓；选项C过于片面且未提及文章强调的结构性因素；选项D错误，文章指出还需要文化转变。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. It continued to shrink at the same rapid rate.\", \"B. It completely disappeared.\", \"C. Progress slowed dramatically, and in some years it even widened slightly.\", \"D. It remained exactly the same every year.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what happened to the gender pay gap after the mid-1990s?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文明确提到“Since the mid-1990s, progress on closing the gender pay gap has slowed dramatically... in some years, the gap even widened slightly”，因此选项C正确。选项A与原文相反；选项B未发生；选项D过于绝对，与“widened slightly”矛盾。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. They are generally paid more than male-dominated professions.\", \"B. They require less education and skill than male-dominated professions.\", \"C. They have historically been undervalued and underpaid compared to male-dominated jobs with similar requirements.\", \"D. They are the only reason for the gender pay gap.\"], \"question\": \"Based on the passage, which of the following can be inferred about occupations dominated by women?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章指出“occupations dominated by women... have historically been undervalued and underpaid relative to male-dominated professions requiring similar levels of education and skill”，因此可以推断这些职业被低估且薪酬较低，选项C正确。选项A与原文相反；选项B未提及；选项D过于绝对，文章还提到了家庭责任等其他因素。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The gender pay gap has been shrinking steadily since the 1980s.\", \"B. The gender pay gap stopped shrinking in the mid-1990s due to several factors, including family responsibilities and occupational undervaluation.\", \"C. Women are paid less than men because they choose lower-paying jobs.\", \"D. The gender pay gap will disappear automatically with better workplace policies.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讨论了性别薪酬差距在20世纪80年代快速缩小，但自90年代中期以来停滞不前，并分析了主要原因（家庭责任和职业价值低估），因此选项B正确概括了主旨。选项A错误，因为90年代中期后进展放缓；选项C过于片面且未提及文章强调的结构性因素；选项D错误，文章指出还需要文化转变。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The gender pay gap has been shrinking steadily since the 1980s.\", \"B. The gender pay gap stopped shrinking in the mid-1990s due to several factors, including family responsibilities and occupational undervaluation.\", \"C. Women are paid less than men because they choose lower-paying jobs.\", \"D. The gender pay gap will disappear automatically with better workplace policies.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讨论了性别薪酬差距在20世纪80年代快速缩小，但自90年代中期以来停滞不前，并分析了主要原因（家庭责任和职业价值低估），因此选项B正确概括了主旨。选项A错误，因为90年代中期后进展放缓；选项C过于片面且未提及文章强调的结构性因素；选项D错误，文章指出还需要文化转变。\"}]'),(41,'en','Eating Meat and the Environment','Yes, eating meat affects the environment, but cows are not killing the climate. This provocative statement captures the complexity of the debate around meat consumption and climate change. Much of the public discussion has been shaped by a 2006 United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) report, which concluded that farm animals were producing more greenhouse gases than all modes of transportation combined. The statistic was startling and was widely cited by environmentalists urging people to reduce their meat consumption for the sake of the planet. But there was a problem. The FAO\'s comparison was methodologically flawed: it used a full lifecycle analysis for livestock but only a partial analysis for transportation. When the error was pointed out, the FAO admitted its mistake, a rare instance of an international organization acknowledging an error. Updated research has since shown that while livestock do contribute significantly to greenhouse gas emissions, their contribution is considerably less than that of the transportation sector in developed countries. In the United States, even if every American were to stop eating meat entirely, the reduction in national greenhouse gas emissions would be relatively modest, perhaps around 2.6 percent. This does not mean that meat consumption is without environmental consequences. It is an energy-intensive way to produce calories, and industrial livestock farming has serious local environmental impacts. But the claim that giving up meat is a cure-all for climate change does not hold up to scrutiny. A more nuanced approach would focus on sustainable farming practices and recognize that more than half of the world\'s agricultural land is suitable only for grazing animals, not for growing crops.',420,NULL,NULL,'专业人士','environment,food,science','2026-07-02 12:33:06',5,'[{\"word\": \"provocative\", \"phonetic\": \"/prəˈvɒkətɪv/\", \"definition\": \"引发争议的，挑衅性的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"methodologically\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌmeθədəˈlɒdʒɪkli/\", \"definition\": \"方法论上地\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adverb\"}, {\"word\": \"lifecycle analysis\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈlaɪfˌsaɪkl əˈnæləsɪs/\", \"definition\": \"生命周期分析\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}, {\"word\": \"livestock\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈlaɪvstɒk/\", \"definition\": \"家畜，牲畜\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"emissions\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪˈmɪʃnz/\", \"definition\": \"排放物，排放量\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"scrutiny\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈskruːtəni/\", \"definition\": \"仔细审查，严密监督\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"nuanced\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈnjuːɑːnst/\", \"definition\": \"细致入微的，有细微差别的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"sustainable\", \"phonetic\": \"/səˈsteɪnəbl/\", \"definition\": \"可持续的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Eating meat is the primary cause of climate change.\", \"B. The environmental impact of meat consumption is often overstated in public debate.\", \"C. The FAO report correctly proved that livestock produce more greenhouse gases than transportation.\", \"D. Giving up meat is the only way to solve climate change.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出‘cows are not killing the climate’，随后通过分析FAO报告的方法论错误和后续研究，说明肉类消费对气候的影响被夸大，因此主旨是‘肉类消费的环境影响在公共讨论中常被夸大’（选项B）。选项A和D与文章结论相反，选项C与事实不符（FAO报告有误）。\"}, {\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. It compared livestock emissions to transportation emissions using different analysis methods.\", \"B. It ignored the emissions from industrial livestock farming.\", \"C. It only analyzed transportation in developing countries.\", \"D. It overestimated the number of farm animals worldwide.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what was the methodological flaw in the 2006 FAO report?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到‘the FAO\'s comparison was methodologically flawed: it used a full lifecycle analysis for livestock but only a partial analysis for transportation’，即对畜牧业采用全生命周期分析，而对交通部门仅采用部分分析，导致比较不公平。选项A准确概括了这一错误。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. The author believes everyone should become vegetarian immediately.\", \"B. The author thinks the environmental benefits of giving up meat are minimal and not worth considering.\", \"C. The author suggests a more balanced approach that includes sustainable farming and acknowledges land use realities.\", \"D. The author argues that transportation emissions are more important to address than livestock emissions.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred from the passage about the author\'s view on reducing meat consumption?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章结尾指出‘A more nuanced approach would focus on sustainable farming practices and recognize that more than half of the world\'s agricultural land is suitable only for grazing animals’，暗示作者支持更平衡的策略，而非极端素食或完全忽视问题。选项C符合这一推断。选项A与作者观点相反，选项B过于绝对（作者承认肉类消费有环境影响），选项D未在文中明确支持。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Eating meat is the primary cause of climate change.\", \"B. The environmental impact of meat consumption is often overstated in public debate.\", \"C. The FAO report correctly proved that livestock produce more greenhouse gases than transportation.\", \"D. Giving up meat is the only way to solve climate change.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出‘cows are not killing the climate’，随后通过分析FAO报告的方法论错误和后续研究，说明肉类消费对气候的影响被夸大，因此主旨是‘肉类消费的环境影响在公共讨论中常被夸大’（选项B）。选项A和D与文章结论相反，选项C与事实不符（FAO报告有误）。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Eating meat is the primary cause of climate change.\", \"B. The environmental impact of meat consumption is often overstated in public debate.\", \"C. The FAO report correctly proved that livestock produce more greenhouse gases than transportation.\", \"D. Giving up meat is the only way to solve climate change.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章开头指出‘cows are not killing the climate’，随后通过分析FAO报告的方法论错误和后续研究，说明肉类消费对气候的影响被夸大，因此主旨是‘肉类消费的环境影响在公共讨论中常被夸大’（选项B）。选项A和D与文章结论相反，选项C与事实不符（FAO报告有误）。\"}]'),(42,'ja','日本の高齢化社会と労働力不足','日本は世界で最も高齢化が進んでいる国の一つである。総務省の統計によると、65歳以上の高齢者が総人口に占める割合は29%を超え、この数字は年々増加している。この急激な高齢化は、労働力不足という深刻な問題を引き起こしている。特に介護や建設、農業などの分野では人手不足が顕著であり、地方の中小企業では廃業を選ぶケースも少なくない。この問題に対して政府は様々な対策を講じている。まず、女性の就業率を高めるための環境整備が進められている。保育所の増設や育児休業制度の拡充、テレワークの推進などが具体例として挙げられる。また、高齢者自身の就労促進も重要な施策である。定年延長や再雇用制度の整備によって、意欲と能力のある高齢者がより長く働き続けられる環境が整えられつつある。さらに、外国人労働者の受け入れ拡大も大きな政策転換といえるだろう。技能実習制度の見直しや、新たな在留資格「特定技能」の創設により、これまでより多くの外国人が日本で働く道が開かれた。しかし、単に労働力の数を増やすだけでは根本的な解決にはならない。生産性の向上こそが長期的な課題である。AI やロボット技術を活用した業務の自動化、デジタルトランスフォーメーションによる業務効率化が急務である。人口減少社会において日本が持続可能な発展を遂げられるかどうかは、こうした技術革新と制度改革の成否にかかっている。',680,NULL,NULL,'N1','society,economy','2026-07-02 12:35:07',4,'[{\"word\": \"高齢化\", \"phonetic\": \"こうれいか\", \"definition\": \"老龄化\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"労働力不足\", \"phonetic\": \"ろうどうりょくぶそく\", \"definition\": \"劳动力不足\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"顕著\", \"phonetic\": \"けんちょ\", \"definition\": \"显著\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"廃業\", \"phonetic\": \"はいぎょう\", \"definition\": \"停业，倒闭\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"施策\", \"phonetic\": \"しさく\", \"definition\": \"措施，对策\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"定年延長\", \"phonetic\": \"ていねんえんちょう\", \"definition\": \"退休年龄延长\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"在留資格\", \"phonetic\": \"ざいりゅうしかく\", \"definition\": \"在留资格（居留许可）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"生産性\", \"phonetic\": \"せいさんせい\", \"definition\": \"生产率\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. 日本の高齢化の現状とそれに伴う労働力不足への対策について論じている。\", \"B. 日本の介護・建設・農業分野における人手不足の実態を報告している。\", \"C. 外国人労働者の受け入れ拡大が日本の労働力不足を解決する唯一の方法である。\", \"D. 日本の人口減少社会において、女性の就業率向上が最も重要な課題である。\"], \"question\": \"この文章の主旨として最も適切なものはどれか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章は高齢化の現状（第1文～第3文）を述べた後、労働力不足への対策として女性就業促進、高齢者就労促進、外国人労働者受け入れを挙げ（第4文～第10文）、最後に生産性向上の必要性を指摘している（第11文～最終文）。Aはこれら全体を包括しており主旨として最適。Bは一部分の詳細に過ぎず、Cは「唯一の方法」と断定している点で誤り、Dも一部分の対策に過ぎない。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 保育所の増設や育児休業制度の拡充\", \"B. 定年延長や再雇用制度の整備\", \"C. 外国人労働者の賃金引き上げの義務化\", \"D. 技能実習制度の見直しや特定技能の創設\"], \"question\": \"政府が行っている労働力不足対策として、文章に含まれていないものはどれか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章ではA（「保育所の増設や育児休業制度の拡充」）、B（「定年延長や再雇用制度の整備」）、D（「技能実習制度の見直しや、新たな在留資格「特定技能」の創設」）が明示されている。Cの「外国人労働者の賃金引き上げの義務化」については本文中に一切言及がない。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 労働力の数を増やすと、かえって高齢化がさらに進むから。\", \"B. 人口減少が続く以上、労働力の絶対数には限界があり、一人当たりの生産性を上げる必要があるから。\", \"C. 外国人労働者を受け入れると、日本の伝統的な労働文化が失われるから。\", \"D. 女性や高齢者の就業率はすでに限界に達しており、これ以上増やすことができないから。\"], \"question\": \"筆者は「単に労働力の数を増やすだけでは根本的な解決にはならない」と述べているが、その理由として最も適切な推測はどれか。\", \"explanation\": \"筆者は「生産性の向上こそが長期的な課題である」と述べ、AIやロボット技術による自動化・効率化を挙げている。これは、人口減少社会では労働力の量的確保には限界があり、質的向上（生産性向上）が不可欠であるという論理に基づく。Bはこの文脈に合致する。Aは因果関係が逆で誤り、Cは本文にない文化的懸念、Dは「すでに限界」という事実は本文に示されていない。\"}]'),(43,'ja','日本人のおもてなし文化','日本を訪れる外国人観光客が最も感動することの一つは、日本のおもてなしの心である。「おもてなし」とは単なるサービス以上のものであり、相手の立場に立って心を込めて対応することを意味する。この精神は、旅館で靴をそろえてくれる仲居さん、タクシーの自動ドア、デパートのエレベーターガールの丁寧なお辞儀など、日常生活のさまざまな場面で見ることができる。おもてなしの根源には、茶道の精神があると言われている。千利休が完成させた侘び茶の精神は、「一期一会」——つまり、全ての出会いは一生に一度だけのものであり、その一瞬一瞬を大切にしなければならないという考え方に基づいている。また、日本には「言わぬが花」という言葉があるように、あえて言葉にしないことで相手を思いやる文化も存在する。しかし、おもてなし文化は変化を迫られている。近年の労働力不足やコスト削減の圧力の中で、過剰なサービスを見直す動きも出てきている。また、外国人労働者の増加に伴い、おもてなしの精神をどのように共有・継承していくかという新たな課題も生まれている。',590,NULL,NULL,'N3','culture,tradition','2026-07-02 12:35:23',2,'[{\"word\": \"おもてなし\", \"phonetic\": \"おもてなし\", \"definition\": \"款待；用心招待\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"仲居\", \"phonetic\": \"なかい\", \"definition\": \"（旅馆等的）女服务员\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"茶道\", \"phonetic\": \"さどう\", \"definition\": \"茶道\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"一期一会\", \"phonetic\": \"いちごいちえ\", \"definition\": \"一期一会；一生只有一次的相遇\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"侘び茶\", \"phonetic\": \"わびちゃ\", \"definition\": \"侘茶；简朴的茶道\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"言わぬが花\", \"phonetic\": \"いわぬがはな\", \"definition\": \"不说为妙；沉默是金\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"思いやる\", \"phonetic\": \"おもいやる\", \"definition\": \"体谅；关怀\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"継承\", \"phonetic\": \"けいしょう\", \"definition\": \"继承；传承\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 日本の観光業の現状と問題点\", \"B. 日本のおもてなしの心とその背景、変化\", \"C. 茶道の歴史と千利休の功績\", \"D. 外国人観光客が日本で感動する場所\"], \"question\": \"この文章の主なテーマは何ですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章全体を通して、日本のおもてなしの心の具体例、その根源にある茶道や一期一会の精神、そして現在直面している変化や課題について述べられています。選択肢Bが最も適切です。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 同じ相手とは何度も会うことができるので、その都度気を遣う必要はない。\", \"B. すべての出会いは一生に一度だけなので、その瞬間を大切にしなければならない。\", \"C. 茶道の世界だけで使われる特別な考え方である。\", \"D. 言葉にしないことで相手を思いやることを意味する。\"], \"question\": \"「一期一会」の考え方として、文章の内容に合っているものはどれですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章では「一期一会」について「全ての出会いは一生に一度だけのものであり、その一瞬一瞬を大切にしなければならないという考え方」と説明されています。選択肢Bが正しいです。\"}, {\"answer\": 3, \"options\": [\"A. 日本のおもてなし文化は、今後もまったく変わらずに続いていく。\", \"B. 外国人労働者の増加は、おもてなしの継承にプラスの影響しか与えない。\", \"C. 日本では、サービスを言葉で細かく説明することが最も重要視されている。\", \"D. おもてなし文化は、労働力不足やコスト削減の影響を受けて変化しつつある。\"], \"question\": \"文章の内容から推測できることとして、最も適切なものはどれですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章の後半で「おもてなし文化は変化を迫られている」「過剰なサービスを見直す動き」「外国人労働者の増加に伴い、おもてなしの精神をどのように共有・継承していくかという新たな課題」と述べられており、変化の兆しがあることが推測できます。選択肢Dが最も適切です。\"}]'),(44,'ja','日本語の敬語と人間関係','日本語の難しさの一つとして、敬語の使い分けがよく挙げられる。敬語には尊敬語、謙譲語、丁寧語の三種類があり、それぞれ使用する場面や相手によって正しく使い分ける必要がある。尊敬語は相手を高める表現であり、「いらっしゃる」「おっしゃる」などがこれにあたる。謙譲語は自分を低めることで相手を敬う表現であり、「申し上げる」「参る」などが含まれる。丁寧語は「です」「ます」を基本とする、改まった場面で使われる表現である。この敬語の体系は、日本社会の縦の人間関係と密接に結びついている。目上の人に対しては自然と敬語を使い、同僚には丁寧語、親しい友人にはため口というように、人間関係の距離感を言葉で表現するのである。しかし、若い世代を中心に敬語の簡略化が進んでいるという指摘もある。アルバイト先で見られる「です・ます調」と「ため口」の中間のような新しい話し方も登場している。',430,NULL,NULL,'N3','language,culture','2026-07-02 12:35:37',2,'[{\"word\": \"敬語\", \"phonetic\": \"けいご\", \"definition\": \"敬语\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"尊敬語\", \"phonetic\": \"そんけいご\", \"definition\": \"尊敬语\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"謙譲語\", \"phonetic\": \"けんじょうご\", \"definition\": \"谦让语\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"丁寧語\", \"phonetic\": \"ていねいご\", \"definition\": \"礼貌语\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"使い分ける\", \"phonetic\": \"つかいわける\", \"definition\": \"区分使用\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"目上\", \"phonetic\": \"めうえ\", \"definition\": \"长辈、上级\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"ため口\", \"phonetic\": \"ためぐち\", \"definition\": \"平辈用语、随意语气\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"簡略化\", \"phonetic\": \"かんりゃくか\", \"definition\": \"简化\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. 日本語の敬語の種類とその社会的な役割について\", \"B. 敬語を正しく使うための練習方法について\", \"C. 若い世代の日本語能力の低下について\", \"D. 日本社会の縦の人間関係の問題点について\"], \"question\": \"この文章の主な内容は何ですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章は敬語の三種類（尊敬語・謙譲語・丁寧語）を説明し、それが日本社会の人間関係と結びついていること、さらに若い世代での変化について述べています。選択肢Aが最も内容を包括しています。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 相手を高める表現で、「いらっしゃる」などがある。\", \"B. 自分を低めることで相手を敬う表現で、「参る」などがある。\", \"C. 改まった場面で使われる表現で、「です」「ます」が基本である。\", \"D. 親しい友人との会話で使われる表現である。\"], \"question\": \"「謙譲語」の説明として正しいものはどれですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章では「謙譲語は自分を低めることで相手を敬う表現であり、『申し上げる』『参る』などが含まれる」と説明されています。選択肢Bが正しいです。Aは尊敬語、Cは丁寧語の説明です。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 敬語のルールは今後も全く変わらないだろう。\", \"B. 日本では全ての人が常に正しい敬語を使っている。\", \"C. 現代の日本では、新しい種類の話し方も生まれている。\", \"D. 敬語はアルバイト先でしか使われなくなっている。\"], \"question\": \"文章の内容から推測できることとして、最も適切なものはどれですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章の最後に「若い世代を中心に敬語の簡略化が進んでいる」「アルバイト先で見られる『です・ます調』と『ため口』の中間のような新しい話し方も登場している」とあることから、新しい話し方が生まれていると推測できます。\"}]'),(45,'ja','留学生活：日本での初めての経験','私は留学生として日本に来てから、もうすぐ一年になる。最初の一ヶ月は本当に大変だった。言葉の壁だけではなく、生活習慣の違いにも戸惑うことが多かったからだ。例えば、ゴミの分別だ。燃えるゴミ、燃えないゴミ、資源ゴミを細かく分ける日本のルールは、私の国にはないものだった。最初はどれがどのゴミかわからず、近所の人に怒られたこともある。しかし、今ではすっかり慣れて、分別しないとかえって気持ち悪く感じるようになった。スーパーで買い物をするときも、お釣りをくれるときにお店の人が必ず両手で渡してくれるのは、最初は驚いたが、今では日本の良さの一つだと思う。日本語学校でできた友達と一緒に、花見や夏祭りにも行った。特に花見の時、満開の桜の下でお弁当を食べたことは忘れられない思い出だ。',360,NULL,NULL,'N5','daily,life,study','2026-07-02 12:35:50',0,'[{\"word\": \"留学生\", \"phonetic\": \"りゅうがくせい\", \"definition\": \"留学生\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"言葉の壁\", \"phonetic\": \"ことばのかべ\", \"definition\": \"语言障碍\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"生活習慣\", \"phonetic\": \"せいかつしゅうかん\", \"definition\": \"生活习惯\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"ゴミの分別\", \"phonetic\": \"ゴミのぶんべつ\", \"definition\": \"垃圾分类\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"慣れる\", \"phonetic\": \"なれる\", \"definition\": \"习惯\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"お釣り\", \"phonetic\": \"おつり\", \"definition\": \"找零\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"花見\", \"phonetic\": \"はなみ\", \"definition\": \"赏花\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"忘れられない\", \"phonetic\": \"わすれられない\", \"definition\": \"难以忘怀的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 日本のゴミの分別方法について\", \"B. 留学生が日本で経験したことと感じた変化\", \"C. 日本の花見と夏祭りの楽しみ方\", \"D. 日本語学校の友達との思い出\"], \"question\": \"この文章の主な内容は何ですか。\", \"explanation\": \"文章全体を通して、留学生が日本に来てからの困難や慣れ、日本の良さを感じた経験が述べられています。ゴミ分別やお店の対応、花見などの具体例は、その変化を説明するためのものです。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 日本語が話せなかったこと\", \"B. 近所の人に怒られたこと\", \"C. ゴミの分別のルールがわからなかったこと\", \"D. スーパーでの買い物の仕方がわからなかったこと\"], \"question\": \"筆者が最初に困ったことは何ですか。\", \"explanation\": \"本文に「最初はどれがどのゴミかわからず、近所の人に怒られたこともある」とあり、ゴミの分別に困ったことが明記されています。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 今でも難しくて困っている\", \"B. まだ慣れていない\", \"C. しないと気持ち悪いと感じるようになった\", \"D. 近所の人がやってくれるので自分はしなくなった\"], \"question\": \"筆者は今、日本のゴミ分別についてどのように感じていますか。\", \"explanation\": \"本文に「今ではすっかり慣れて、分別しないとかえって気持ち悪く感じるようになった」とあり、筆者がポジティブに変化したことがわかります。\"}]'),(46,'ko','한국의 교육열과 그 사회적 영향','한국은 세계적으로 유명한 교육열을 가진 나라이다. OECD 통계에 따르면 한국의 GDP 대비 교육비 지출 비율은 상위권에 속하며, 사교육 시장 규모도 매년 증가하고 있다. 초등학생부터 고등학생에 이르기까지 많은 학생들이 학교 수업이 끝난 후 학원으로 향한다. 이러한 교육열은 경제 성장의 원동력이 되었다는 긍정적인 평가를 받기도 한다. 실제로 한국의 높은 교육 수준은 국가 경쟁력 향상에 크게 기여했다. 그러나 교육열의 이면에는 심각한 사회 문제도 존재한다. 과도한 경쟁으로 인한 학생들의 스트레스와 정신 건강 문제가 사회적 이슈로 떠오르고 있으며, 사교육비 부담이 저출산의 원인 중 하나로 지목되고 있다. 교육 기회의 불평등도 중요한 문제이다. 소득 수준에 따라 사교육 접근성이 달라지고, 이는 다시 대학 진학과 취업의 격차로 이어지는 악순환이 발생하고 있는 것이다.',490,NULL,NULL,'5级','society,education','2026-07-02 12:38:47',4,'[{\"word\": \"교육열\", \"phonetic\": \"교육열\", \"definition\": \"教育热\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"사교육\", \"phonetic\": \"사교육\", \"definition\": \"课外教育/补习教育\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"원동력\", \"phonetic\": \"원동력\", \"definition\": \"原动力\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"경쟁력\", \"phonetic\": \"경쟁력\", \"definition\": \"竞争力\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"이면\", \"phonetic\": \"이면\", \"definition\": \"另一面/背面\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"저출산\", \"phonetic\": \"저출산\", \"definition\": \"低生育率\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"불평등\", \"phonetic\": \"불평등\", \"definition\": \"不平等\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"악순환\", \"phonetic\": \"악순환\", \"definition\": \"恶性循环\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 한국의 교육열이 경제 성장에만 긍정적인 영향을 미쳤다.\", \"B. 한국의 교육열은 긍정적 측면과 부정적 측면을 동시에 지니고 있다.\", \"C. 한국의 사교육 시장 규모가 OECD 국가 중 가장 크다.\", \"D. 한국의 교육열은 저출산 문제와 전혀 관련이 없다.\"], \"question\": \"이 글의 중심 내용으로 가장 적절한 것은?\", \"explanation\": \"이 글은 한국의 교육열이 경제 성장에 기여한 긍정적 측면과 함께 과도한 경쟁, 정신 건강 문제, 사교육비 부담, 교육 불평등 등 부정적 측면을 함께 제시하고 있으므로, 중심 내용은 교육열의 양면성이다.\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 한국의 대학 진학률\", \"B. 한국의 GDP 대비 교육비 지출 비율이 OECD 상위권이라는 점\", \"C. 한국 학생들의 1인당 사교육비 평균 금액\", \"D. 한국의 저출산율과 사교육비의 상관관계 수치\"], \"question\": \"다음 중 한국의 교육열과 관련하여 본문에서 언급된 구체적인 통계는 무엇인가?\", \"explanation\": \"본문에서 \'OECD 통계에 따르면 한국의 GDP 대비 교육비 지출 비율은 상위권에 속한다\'고 직접 언급되었으며, 다른 보기들은 본문에 구체적인 수치나 통계로 제시되지 않았다.\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 소득 수준이 낮은 가정의 학생들이 학업을 포기하는 경우가 많기 때문에\", \"B. 소득에 따른 사교육 접근성 차이가 대학 진학과 취업 격차로 이어져 불평등이 재생산되기 때문에\", \"C. 정부가 교육 불평등을 해결하기 위한 정책을 전혀 시행하지 않고 있기 때문에\", \"D. 고소득 가정의 학생들만 해외 유학을 갈 수 있기 때문에\"], \"question\": \"글쓴이가 \'교육 기회의 불평등\'을 \'악순환\'이라고 표현한 이유로 가장 적절한 것은?\", \"explanation\": \"본문에서 \'소득 수준에 따라 사교육 접근성이 달라지고, 이는 다시 대학 진학과 취업의 격차로 이어지는 악순환\'이라고 설명하고 있으므로, 불평등이 고착화되어 반복된다는 의미에서 악순환으로 표현한 것이다.\"}]'),(47,'ko','K-푸드와 세계 속의 한국 음식','최근 몇 년 사이에 한국 음식이 세계적으로 큰 인기를 얻고 있다. 라면과 김치는 이미 오래전부터 해외에서 사랑받아 왔지만, 최근에는 떡볶이, 치킨, 불고기 등도 전 세계인의 입맛을 사로잡고 있다. 한국 음식이 이렇게 인기를 얻게 된 이유는 무엇일까? 첫째, 건강에 좋은 이미지다. 김치, 된장 등 발효 식품이 건강에 좋다는 인식이 세계적으로 확산되면서 한국 음식도 주목을 받게 되었다. 둘째, SNS와 유튜브의 영향이다. 먹방 콘텐츠를 통해 외국인들이 한국 음식을 접하게 되었고, 직접 만들어 보는 사람들도 늘어나고 있다. 셋째, 한류의 영향이다. K-POP과 한국 드라마에 등장하는 음식들은 자연스럽게 시청자들의 관심을 끌게 된다.',430,NULL,NULL,'3级','culture,food','2026-07-02 12:39:00',2,'[{\"word\": \"인기\", \"phonetic\": \"in-gi\", \"definition\": \"人气\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"입맛\", \"phonetic\": \"im-mat\", \"definition\": \"口味，食欲\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"사로잡다\", \"phonetic\": \"sa-ro-jap-da\", \"definition\": \"抓住，吸引\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"발효\", \"phonetic\": \"bal-hyo\", \"definition\": \"发酵\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"확산되다\", \"phonetic\": \"hwak-san-doe-da\", \"definition\": \"扩散，传播\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"주목\", \"phonetic\": \"ju-mok\", \"definition\": \"关注，注目\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"먹방\", \"phonetic\": \"meok-bang\", \"definition\": \"吃播（美食直播）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"한류\", \"phonetic\": \"hal-lyu\", \"definition\": \"韩流\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. 한국 음식의 세계적 인기와 그 이유\", \"B. 한국 음식 중 가장 인기 있는 메뉴\", \"C. 건강에 좋은 한국 발효 식품의 종류\", \"D. 먹방 콘텐츠가 한국 경제에 미치는 영향\"], \"question\": \"이 글의 주제로 가장 알맞은 것은?\", \"explanation\": \"이 글은 한국 음식이 세계적으로 인기를 얻고 있는 현상과 그 이유(건강 이미지, SNS, 한류)를 설명하고 있으므로 주제는 \'한국 음식의 세계적 인기와 그 이유\'입니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 3, \"options\": [\"A. 발효 식품의 건강 이미지\", \"B. SNS와 유튜브 먹방 콘텐츠\", \"C. K-POP과 드라마의 영향\", \"D. 한국 음식의 가격이 저렴해서\"], \"question\": \"글에 따르면, 한국 음식이 세계적으로 인기를 얻게 된 이유가 아닌 것은?\", \"explanation\": \"글에서는 건강 이미지, SNS/유튜브, 한류의 세 가지 이유를 들었습니다. 가격이 저렴하다는 내용은 언급되지 않았습니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 한국 음식이 맛있어 보이지 않는다는 점을 지적하려고\", \"B. 외국인들이 한국 음식을 직접 만들어 먹는 사례를 소개하려고\", \"C. SNS가 한국 음식의 세계적 확산에 기여했음을 설명하려고\", \"D. 먹방이 한국 전통 음식을 왜곡한다고 비판하려고\"], \"question\": \"글쓴이가 \'먹방 콘텐츠\'를 언급한 의도로 가장 알맞은 것은?\", \"explanation\": \"글쓴이는 SNS와 유튜브의 영향 중 하나로 먹방 콘텐츠를 통해 외국인들이 한국 음식을 접하게 되었다고 설명하며, 이것이 한국 음식의 인기 확산에 기여했음을 나타내고 있습니다.\"}]'),(48,'ko','도서관에서의 하루','저는 주말마다 우리 동네 도서관에 갑니다. 도서관은 집에서 걸어서 십 분 정도 걸립니다. 조용하고 깨끗한 곳이라서 공부하기에 아주 좋습니다. 아침 아홉 시에 도서관에 도착하면, 이미 많은 사람들이 와 있습니다. 저는 평소에 좋아하는 자리, 즉 창가 쪽 자리에 앉습니다. 거기에서는 바깥 정원도 보이고 햇빛도 잘 들어서 기분이 좋습니다. 오전에는 주로 영어 단어를 외우거나 책을 읽습니다. 점심 시간이 되면 일 층에 있는 작은 카페에 가서 샌드위치를 사 먹습니다. 가끔은 도시락을 싸 가지고 가기도 합니다. 오후에는 한국어 문법 공부를 합니다. 한국어는 배우면 배울수록 재미있습니다. 처음에는 한글도 몰랐는데, 지금은 한국 드라마를 자막 없이 볼 수 있을 정도가 되었습니다. 저녁 여섯 시쯤 집에 돌아오면 기분이 뿌듯합니다.',350,NULL,NULL,'1级','daily,life,study','2026-07-02 12:39:13',0,'[{\"word\": \"도서관\", \"phonetic\": \"do-seo-gwan\", \"definition\": \"图书馆\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"걸리다\", \"phonetic\": \"geol-li-da\", \"definition\": \"花费（时间）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"조용하다\", \"phonetic\": \"jo-yong-ha-da\", \"definition\": \"安静\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"도착하다\", \"phonetic\": \"do-chak-ha-da\", \"definition\": \"到达\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"자리\", \"phonetic\": \"ja-ri\", \"definition\": \"座位\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"외우다\", \"phonetic\": \"oe-u-da\", \"definition\": \"背诵\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"문법\", \"phonetic\": \"mun-beop\", \"definition\": \"语法\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"뿌듯하다\", \"phonetic\": \"ppu-deut-ha-da\", \"definition\": \"充满成就感/欣慰\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 도서관에서 공부하는 방법\", \"B. 주말에 도서관에서 보내는 하루\", \"C. 한국어 공부의 어려움\", \"D. 도서관 카페의 음식\"], \"question\": \"이 글의 주제는 무엇입니까?\", \"explanation\": \"이 글은 주말마다 도서관에 가서 공부하고 점심을 먹고 저녁에 돌아오는 하루 일과를 설명하고 있습니다. 따라서 주제는 \'주말에 도서관에서 보내는 하루\'입니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 항상 카페에서 샌드위치를 삽니다.\", \"B. 항상 도시락을 싸 갑니다.\", \"C. 가끔 도시락을 싸 가기도 합니다.\", \"D. 집에 가서 밥을 먹습니다.\"], \"question\": \"저자가 도서관에서 점심을 먹을 때 하는 것은 무엇입니까?\", \"explanation\": \"글에 \'점심 시간이 되면 일 층에 있는 작은 카페에 가서 샌드위치를 사 먹습니다. 가끔은 도시락을 싸 가지고 가기도 합니다.\'라고 나와 있습니다. 따라서 가끔 도시락을 싸 간다는 것이 맞습니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 아직 한글을 모릅니다.\", \"B. 한국 드라마를 자막 없이 볼 수 있습니다.\", \"C. 한국어가 너무 어려워서 포기했습니다.\", \"D. 한국어 문법만 공부합니다.\"], \"question\": \"저자의 한국어 실력에 대해 알 수 있는 것은 무엇입니까?\", \"explanation\": \"글에 \'처음에는 한글도 몰랐는데, 지금은 한국 드라마를 자막 없이 볼 수 있을 정도가 되었습니다.\'라고 나와 있습니다. 따라서 한국 드라마를 자막 없이 볼 수 있다는 것을 알 수 있습니다.\"}]'),(49,'ko','도시와 시골 생활 비교','도시 생활과 시골 생활은 각각 장점과 단점이 있습니다. 도시는 모든 것이 가까이에 있어서 편리합니다. 좋은 병원도 많고, 학교도 많으며, 지하철이나 버스 같은 대중교통도 잘 되어 있습니다. 또 영화관이나 쇼핑몰 같은 즐길 거리도 많습니다. 하지만 단점도 적지 않습니다. 특히 집값이 비싸고 공기가 깨끗하지 않은 것이 큰 문제입니다. 반면에 시골 생활은 자연과 가까워서 공기가 맑고 경치가 아름답습니다. 직접 기른 채소를 먹을 수도 있고, 이웃 간의 정이 두터워 외롭지 않습니다. 하지만 취업 기회가 적고, 문화 시설이 부족하다는 점에서는 도시보다 불편한 것이 사실입니다.',310,NULL,NULL,'1级','daily,life','2026-07-02 12:39:26',0,'[{\"word\": \"도시\", \"phonetic\": \"do-si\", \"definition\": \"城市\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"시골\", \"phonetic\": \"si-gol\", \"definition\": \"乡村\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"편리하다\", \"phonetic\": \"pyeol-li-ha-da\", \"definition\": \"方便\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"대중교통\", \"phonetic\": \"dae-jung-gyo-tong\", \"definition\": \"公共交通\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"집값\", \"phonetic\": \"jip-gap\", \"definition\": \"房价\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"자연\", \"phonetic\": \"ja-yeon\", \"definition\": \"自然\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"맑다\", \"phonetic\": \"mak-da\", \"definition\": \"清新/晴朗\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"이웃\", \"phonetic\": \"i-ut\", \"definition\": \"邻居\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. 도시와 시골의 교통 비교\", \"B. 도시 생활과 시골 생활의 장단점\", \"C. 시골에서 채소를 기르는 방법\", \"D. 도시의 집값 문제\"], \"question\": \"이 글의 주제는 무엇인가요?\", \"explanation\": \"이 글은 도시 생활과 시골 생활의 장점과 단점을 각각 설명하고 있습니다. \'도시 생활과 시골 생활은 각각 장점과 단점이 있습니다\'라는 첫 문장에서 주제를 알 수 있습니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 대중교통이 불편하다\", \"B. 이웃 간의 정이 두텁다\", \"C. 집값이 비싸고 공기가 깨끗하지 않다\", \"D. 문화 시설이 부족하다\"], \"question\": \"글에 따르면, 도시 생활의 단점은 무엇인가요?\", \"explanation\": \"글에서 \'특히 집값이 비싸고 공기가 깨끗하지 않은 것이 큰 문제입니다\'라고 도시 생활의 단점을 설명하고 있습니다.\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 시골은 취업 기회가 많다\", \"B. 시골은 도시보다 모든 면에서 편리하다\", \"C. 시골에서는 자연과 가까운 생활을 할 수 있다\", \"D. 시골에는 영화관이나 쇼핑몰이 많다\"], \"question\": \"시골 생활에 대해 글에서 말하고 있는 내용으로 알맞은 것은 무엇인가요?\", \"explanation\": \"글에서 \'시골 생활은 자연과 가까워서 공기가 맑고 경치가 아름답습니다\'라고 했으므로, 시골에서는 자연과 가까운 생활을 할 수 있다는 것을 알 수 있습니다. 다른 보기들은 글의 내용과 반대되거나 언급되지 않았습니다.\"}]'),(50,'fr','La réforme des retraites en France','La question des retraites est l\'un des sujets les plus debattus dans la societe francaise contemporaine. Le systeme de retraite francais, fonde sur le principe de la repartition, permet aux actifs de financer les pensions des retraites actuels. Ce systeme repose sur un equilibre demographique fragile: il faut suffisamment de cotisants pour financer les pensions. Or, avec l\'allongement de l\'esperance de vie et le vieillissement de la population, cet equilibre est menace. Le gouvernement a propose plusieurs reformes pour garantir la perennite du systeme. La mesure la plus controversee est le report de l\'age legal de depart a la retraite de 62 a 64 ans. Cette proposition a suscite de vives oppositions de la part des syndicats et une partie importante de la population. Des manifestations massives ont ete organisees dans tout le pays, rassemblant parfois plus d\'un million de personnes. Les opposants a la reforme estiment qu\'elle penalise injustement les travailleurs qui ont commence leur carriere tot et ceux qui exercent des metiers physiquement exigeants.',580,NULL,NULL,'C1','society,politics','2026-07-02 12:39:40',4,'[{\"word\": \"la répartition\", \"phonetic\": \"/la ʁe.paʁ.ti.sjɔ̃/\", \"definition\": \"分摊制（现收现付制）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"l\'équilibre démographique\", \"phonetic\": \"/le.ki.libʁ de.mo.ɡʁa.fik/\", \"definition\": \"人口平衡\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"le cotisant\", \"phonetic\": \"/lə kɔ.ti.zɑ̃/\", \"definition\": \"缴费者（社保缴纳人）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"la pérennité\", \"phonetic\": \"/la pe.ʁe.ni.te/\", \"definition\": \"持久性，可持续性\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"le report\", \"phonetic\": \"/lə ʁə.pɔʁ/\", \"definition\": \"推迟，延迟\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"suscite\", \"phonetic\": \"/sy.sit/\", \"definition\": \"引起，激起\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"les syndicats\", \"phonetic\": \"/le sɛ̃.di.ka/\", \"definition\": \"工会\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"pénalise\", \"phonetic\": \"/pe.na.liz/\", \"definition\": \"惩罚，使处于不利地位\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Le système de retraite français est entièrement privatisé.\", \"B. Le système de retraite français, basé sur la répartition, est menacé par des facteurs démographiques et suscite des débats autour des réformes.\", \"C. Le gouvernement a supprimé l\'âge légal de départ à la retraite.\", \"D. Les syndicats soutiennent pleinement le report de l\'âge légal de la retraite.\"], \"question\": \"Quelle est l\'idée principale du texte ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要介绍了法国退休制度基于现收现付制，面临人口老龄化等威胁，政府提出改革（如提高退休年龄）引发争议，因此B项最符合主旨。A项错误，文中未提及私有化；C项错误，政府是推迟退休年龄而非取消；D项错误，工会强烈反对改革。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. 60 ans\", \"B. 62 ans\", \"C. 64 ans\", \"D. 65 ans\"], \"question\": \"Selon le texte, quel est l\'âge légal de départ à la retraite proposé par la réforme ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到“le report de l\'âge légal de départ à la retraite de 62 à 64 ans”，即从62岁推迟到64岁，因此改革提议的法定退休年龄为64岁。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Parce qu\'elle augmente les pensions des retraités actuels.\", \"B. Parce qu\'elle ne tient pas compte des carrières longues et des métiers pénibles.\", \"C. Parce qu\'elle réduit le nombre de cotisants.\", \"D. Parce qu\'elle est soutenue par tous les syndicats.\"], \"question\": \"Pourquoi peut-on déduire que les opposants à la réforme considèrent celle-ci comme injuste ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到“Les opposants à la réforme estiment qu\'elle penalise injustement les travailleurs qui ont commence leur carriere tot et ceux qui exercent des metiers physiquement exigeants”，即反对者认为改革不公平地惩罚了早年开始职业生涯和从事体力要求高的工作的人，因此可推断出B项正确。\"}]'),(51,'fr','La gastronomie francaise: un patrimoine vivant','La gastronomie francaise est inscrite au patrimoine culturel immateriel de l\'UNESCO depuis 2010. Cette reconnaissance temoigne de l\'importance de la cuisine dans la culture francaise. Le repas gastronomique francais n\'est pas seulement une question de nourriture: c\'est un rituel social qui reunit famille et amis autour d\'une table. Un repas traditionnel se compose generalement de plusieurs plats: l\'entree, le plat principal, le fromage et le dessert, le tout accompagne de pain et de vin. Chaque region de France possede ses propres specialites culinaires. En Bretagne, on deguste des crepes et des galettes. En Alsace, la choucroute est incontournable. Dans le Sud-Ouest, le foie gras et le confit de canard font la fierte de la region.',420,NULL,NULL,'B1','culture,food','2026-07-02 12:39:53',2,'[{\"word\": \"gastronomie\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɡas.tʁɔ.nɔ.mi/\", \"definition\": \"美食学；烹饪法\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"patrimoine\", \"phonetic\": \"/pa.tʁi.mwan/\", \"definition\": \"遗产；财富\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"reconnaissance\", \"phonetic\": \"/ʁə.kɔ.nɛ.sɑ̃s/\", \"definition\": \"承认；认可\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"rituel\", \"phonetic\": \"/ʁi.tɥɛl/\", \"definition\": \"仪式；惯例\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"se composer de\", \"phonetic\": \"/sə kɔ̃.po.ze də/\", \"definition\": \"由……组成\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"spécialité\", \"phonetic\": \"/spe.sja.li.te/\", \"definition\": \"特产；特色菜\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"déguster\", \"phonetic\": \"/de.ɡys.te/\", \"definition\": \"品尝；品味\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"incontournable\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɛ̃.kɔ̃.tuʁ.nabl/\", \"definition\": \"不可错过的；必不可少的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. La gastronomie française est reconnue par l\'UNESCO et représente un rituel social important.\", \"B. Les Français mangent toujours du pain et du vin à chaque repas.\", \"C. Chaque région de France a les mêmes spécialités culinaires.\", \"D. Le repas gastronomique français est uniquement une question de nourriture.\"], \"question\": \"Quelle est l\'idée principale du texte ?\", \"explanation\": \"Le texte explique que la gastronomie française est inscrite à l\'UNESCO et qu\'il s\'agit d\'un rituel social, ce qui correspond à l\'option A. Les autres options sont fausses car le texte mentionne des spécialités régionales différentes et précise que ce n\'est pas seulement une question de nourriture.\"}, {\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. L\'entrée, le plat principal, le fromage et le dessert.\", \"B. La choucroute, les crêpes et le foie gras.\", \"C. Un seul plat principal sans accompagnement.\", \"D. Uniquement du pain et du vin.\"], \"question\": \"Selon le texte, quels plats trouve-t-on traditionnellement dans un repas gastronomique français ?\", \"explanation\": \"Le texte indique clairement qu\'un repas traditionnel se compose de l\'entrée, du plat principal, du fromage et du dessert, accompagnés de pain et de vin. L\'option A est donc correcte. Les options B et D sont des exemples régionaux ou des accompagnements, et l\'option C est incorrecte.\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Parce que les Français ne mangent que des plats régionaux.\", \"B. Parce que c\'est un rituel social qui rassemble famille et amis.\", \"C. Parce que l\'UNESCO a interdit la cuisine française.\", \"D. Parce que chaque repas doit obligatoirement contenir du foie gras.\"], \"question\": \"Pourquoi peut-on dire que la gastronomie française est plus qu\'un simple repas ?\", \"explanation\": \"Le texte précise que le repas gastronomique français est un rituel social qui réunit famille et amis autour d\'une table, ce qui va au-delà de la simple nourriture. L\'option B est donc correcte. Les autres options sont fausses : l\'UNESCO a reconnu la gastronomie, pas interdit, et les plats régionaux ou le foie gras ne sont pas obligatoires.\"}]'),(52,'fr','Ma routine quotidienne','Je m\'appelle Marie et j\'ai vingt-deux ans. Je suis etudiante en lettres modernes a l\'Universite de Lyon. Tous les jours, je me reveille a sept heures du matin. Je prends une douche rapide et je m\'habille. Ensuite, je prepare mon petit-dejeuner: un bol de cafe au lait et une tartine de pain avec du beurre et de la confiture. J\'adore ce moment calme avant de commencer la journee. A huit heures, je quitte mon appartement. J\'habite pres de l\'universite, donc j\'y vais a pied, ce qui me prend environ quinze minutes. Les cours commencent generalement a huit heures et demie. Le matin, j\'ai trois heures de cours. Apres la pause dejeuner, je vais a la bibliotheque universitaire pour etudier. Le soir, je retrouve souvent mes amis dans un petit cafe pres de la place Bellecour.',300,NULL,NULL,'A1','daily,life,school','2026-07-02 12:40:04',0,'[{\"word\": \"s\'appeler\", \"phonetic\": \"s‿ap.le\", \"definition\": \"名叫；被称为\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"étudiant\", \"phonetic\": \"e.ty.djɑ̃\", \"definition\": \"大学生\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"se réveiller\", \"phonetic\": \"sə ʁe.ve.je\", \"definition\": \"醒来\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"petit-déjeuner\", \"phonetic\": \"pə.ti de.ʒœ.ne\", \"definition\": \"早餐\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"habiter\", \"phonetic\": \"a.bi.te\", \"definition\": \"居住\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"à pied\", \"phonetic\": \"a pje\", \"definition\": \"步行\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adv\"}, {\"word\": \"cours\", \"phonetic\": \"kuʁ\", \"definition\": \"课程；课\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"bibliothèque\", \"phonetic\": \"bi.bli.jɔ.tɛk\", \"definition\": \"图书馆\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. La vie quotidienne d\'une étudiante à Lyon\", \"B. Les cours à l\'Université de Lyon\", \"C. Les amis de Marie\", \"D. Le petit-déjeuner français\"], \"question\": \"Quel est le sujet principal de ce texte ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要描述了Marie作为里昂大学现代文学专业学生的一天生活，包括起床、早餐、上课、学习和与朋友见面，因此主旨是\'里昂一名学生的日常生活\'。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. À sept heures\", \"B. À huit heures\", \"C. À huit heures et demie\", \"D. À sept heures et demie\"], \"question\": \"À quelle heure Marie quitte-t-elle son appartement ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到\'A huit heures, je quitte mon appartement\'（八点我离开公寓），因此正确答案是B。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Elle n\'a pas de voiture\", \"B. Elle aime marcher\", \"C. Elle habite près de l\'université\", \"D. Le bus est trop cher\"], \"question\": \"Pourquoi Marie va-t-elle à l\'université à pied ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到\'J\'habite pres de l\'universite, donc j\'y vais a pied\'（我住在大学附近，所以步行去），因此推断原因是她住得近，正确答案是C。\"}]'),(53,'fr','Les vacances ideales en France','Chaque annee, des millions de touristes visitent la France. Certains viennent pour admirer les monuments de Paris comme la Tour Eiffel et le Musee du Louvre. D\'autres preferent les plages de la Cote d\'Azur ou les montagnes des Alpes. J\'habite a Bordeaux, une belle ville dans le sud-ouest de la France, celebre pour son vin. Quand mes amis etrangers me rendent visite, je les emmene d\'abord dans le centre historique. Nous nous promenons le long de la Garonne et nous admirons les beaux batiments du dix-huitieme siecle. Ensuite, nous allons dans un restaurant typique pour gouter la cuisine locale. Le week-end, nous aimons faire une excursion dans les vignobles autour de la ville.',280,NULL,NULL,'A1','travel,daily','2026-07-02 12:40:16',0,'[{\"word\": \"touristes\", \"phonetic\": \"tu.ʁist\", \"definition\": \"游客\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"visiter\", \"phonetic\": \"vi.zi.te\", \"definition\": \"参观；访问\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"monuments\", \"phonetic\": \"mɔ.ny.mɑ̃\", \"definition\": \"纪念碑；历史建筑\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"belle\", \"phonetic\": \"bɛl\", \"definition\": \"美丽的（阴性形式）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"centre historique\", \"phonetic\": \"sɑ̃tʁ is.tɔ.ʁik\", \"definition\": \"历史中心\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"restaurant\", \"phonetic\": \"ʁɛs.tɔ.ʁɑ̃\", \"definition\": \"餐厅\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"cuisine\", \"phonetic\": \"kɥi.zin\", \"definition\": \"烹饪；菜肴\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"excursion\", \"phonetic\": \"ɛk.skyʁ.sjɔ̃\", \"definition\": \"远足；短途旅行\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Les différents types de vins français\", \"B. Le tourisme en France et à Bordeaux\", \"C. Les monuments de Paris uniquement\", \"D. La vie quotidienne dans les Alpes\"], \"question\": \"Quel est le sujet principal de ce texte ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章第一句就提到每年有数百万游客访问法国，接着介绍了巴黎、蔚蓝海岸、阿尔卑斯山等旅游目的地，最后重点描述了作者在波尔多的生活以及带朋友游览的经历。因此，文章主旨是关于法国及波尔多的旅游。选项B正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Dans le nord de la France\", \"B. Sur la Côte d\'Azur\", \"C. Dans le sud-ouest de la France\", \"D. Près des Alpes\"], \"question\": \"Où se trouve Bordeaux ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确写道：“J\'habite à Bordeaux, une belle ville dans le sud-ouest de la France”。因此，波尔多位于法国西南部。选项C正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Parce que ses amis ont faim\", \"B. Pour goûter la cuisine locale\", \"C. Pour admirer les monuments\", \"D. Pour acheter du vin\"], \"question\": \"Pourquoi l\'auteur emmène-t-il ses amis dans un restaurant typique ?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到：“Ensuite, nous allons dans un restaurant typique pour goûter la cuisine locale.” 由此可以推断，作者带朋友去典型餐厅的目的是品尝当地美食。选项B正确。\"}]'),(54,'de','Digitalisierung und Arbeitsmarkt in Deutschland','Die Digitalisierung veraendert den deutschen Arbeitsmarkt grundlegend. Studien des Instituts fuer Arbeitsmarkt- und Berufsforschung zeigen, dass in den kommenden Jahren viele traditionelle Berufe verschwinden oder sich stark veraendern werden. Gleichzeitig entstehen neue Berufsfelder, die vor wenigen Jahren noch nicht existierten. Besonders betroffen sind Taetigkeiten mit hohem Routineanteil, die zunehmend von Maschinen und Algorithmen uebernommen werden koennen. Aber auch qualifizierte Berufe wie Buchhalter oder Juristen sind vom Wandel betroffen, da kuenstliche Intelligenz immer komplexere Aufgaben bewaeltigen kann. Die Bundesregierung hat verschiedene Programme aufgelegt, um den Strukturwandel zu begleiten. Die Foerderung von Weiterbildung und lebenslangem Lernen steht dabei im Mittelpunkt.',530,NULL,NULL,'C1','technology,society','2026-07-02 12:40:30',4,'[{\"word\": \"Digitalisierung\", \"phonetic\": \"ˌdiɡitaliˈziːrʊŋ\", \"definition\": \"数字化\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Arbeitsmarkt\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈaʁbaɪtsˌmaʁkt\", \"definition\": \"劳动力市场\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Routineanteil\", \"phonetic\": \"ʁuˈtiːnʔanˌtaɪl\", \"definition\": \"常规性比例\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Algorithmus\", \"phonetic\": \"alɡoˈʁɪtmʊs\", \"definition\": \"算法\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"künstliche Intelligenz\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈkʏnstlɪçə ɪntɛliˈɡɛnts\", \"definition\": \"人工智能\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Strukturwandel\", \"phonetic\": \"ʃtʁʊkˈtuːɐ̯ˌvandl̩\", \"definition\": \"结构转型\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Weiterbildung\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈvaɪtɐˌbɪldʊŋ\", \"definition\": \"继续教育\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"lebenslanges Lernen\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈleːbn̩slaŋəs ˈlɛʁnən\", \"definition\": \"终身学习\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Die Digitalisierung führt ausschließlich zum Verschwinden von Arbeitsplätzen.\", \"B. Die Digitalisierung verändert den Arbeitsmarkt grundlegend, wobei alte Berufe verschwinden und neue entstehen.\", \"C. Nur gering qualifizierte Berufe sind von der Digitalisierung betroffen.\", \"D. Die Bundesregierung verhindert den Wandel durch neue Gesetze.\"], \"question\": \"Was ist die Hauptaussage des Textes?\", \"explanation\": \"Der Text betont, dass die Digitalisierung den Arbeitsmarkt grundlegend verändert, traditionelle Berufe verschwinden oder sich wandeln und neue Berufsfelder entstehen. Option B fasst diese Hauptaussage korrekt zusammen.\"}, {\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. Berufe mit hohem Routineanteil\", \"B. Nur handwerkliche Berufe\", \"C. Berufe im öffentlichen Dienst\", \"D. Kreative Berufe wie Künstler\"], \"question\": \"Welche Berufsgruppe ist laut Text besonders von der Digitalisierung betroffen?\", \"explanation\": \"Im Text heißt es: \'Besonders betroffen sind Tätigkeiten mit hohem Routineanteil, die zunehmend von Maschinen und Algorithmen übernommen werden können.\' Daher ist Option A korrekt.\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Die Bundesregierung ignoriert den Strukturwandel.\", \"B. Die Bundesregierung versucht, den Wandel durch Förderung von Weiterbildung zu begleiten.\", \"C. Die Bundesregierung verbietet den Einsatz von künstlicher Intelligenz in bestimmten Berufen.\", \"D. Die Bundesregierung konzentriert sich nur auf die Schaffung neuer Arbeitsplätze.\"], \"question\": \"Was kann aus dem Text über die Rolle der Bundesregierung geschlossen werden?\", \"explanation\": \"Der Text erwähnt, dass die Bundesregierung Programme aufgelegt hat, um den Strukturwandel zu begleiten, wobei die Förderung von Weiterbildung und lebenslangem Lernen im Mittelpunkt steht. Dies lässt auf eine aktive Begleitung des Wandels schließen, nicht auf Ignoranz oder Verbote.\"}]'),(55,'de','Das deutsche Schulsystem im Wandel','Das deutsche Bildungssystem befindet sich in einem tiefgreifenden Wandel. Traditionell werden Schueler in Deutschland nach der Grundschule auf verschiedene Schulformen verteilt: Hauptschule, Realschule und Gymnasium. Dieses dreigliedrige System wurde oft wegen seiner fruehen Selektion kritisiert, die Bildungschancen stark von der sozialen Herkunft abhaengig mache. In den letzten Jahren haben viele Bundeslaender Reformen durchgefuehrt. Immer mehr Schulen werden zu Gesamtschulen umgewandelt, in denen alle Kinder gemeinsam lernen. Ein weiteres wichtiges Thema ist die Digitalisierung der Schulen. Waehrend der Corona-Pandemie wurde deutlich, dass viele Schulen in Deutschland technisch nicht ausreichend ausgestattet sind.',420,NULL,NULL,'B1','education,society','2026-07-02 12:40:43',2,'[{\"word\": \"Bildungssystem\", \"phonetic\": \"[ˈbɪldʊŋszʏsteːm]\", \"definition\": \"教育体系\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"tiefgreifend\", \"phonetic\": \"[ˈtiːfɡʁaɪfənt]\", \"definition\": \"深刻的，彻底的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"dreigliedrig\", \"phonetic\": \"[ˈdʁaɪɡliːdʁɪç]\", \"definition\": \"三轨制的，三部分的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adj\"}, {\"word\": \"Selektion\", \"phonetic\": \"[zelekˈt͡si̯oːn]\", \"definition\": \"筛选，选拔\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Bildungschancen\", \"phonetic\": \"[ˈbɪldʊŋsˌʃant͡sn̩]\", \"definition\": \"教育机会\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Herkunft\", \"phonetic\": \"[ˈheːɐ̯kʊnft]\", \"definition\": \"出身，来源\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Gesamtschule\", \"phonetic\": \"[ɡəˈzamtʃuːlə]\", \"definition\": \"综合中学\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Digitalisierung\", \"phonetic\": \"[diɡitaliˈziːʁʊŋ]\", \"definition\": \"数字化\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Die Geschichte des deutschen Schulsystems\", \"B. Aktuelle Veränderungen und Herausforderungen im deutschen Bildungssystem\", \"C. Die Vorteile des dreigliedrigen Schulsystems\", \"D. Die Rolle der Lehrer in deutschen Schulen\"], \"question\": \"Was ist das Hauptthema des Textes?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讨论了德国教育体系的深刻变革，包括从传统的三分制学校体系向综合学校的转变，以及数字化方面的挑战。选项B最准确地概括了文章主旨。选项A（历史）、C（三分制优势）和D（教师角色）均不是文章重点。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Hauptschule\", \"B. Realschule\", \"C. Gesamtschule\", \"D. Gymnasium\"], \"question\": \"Welche Schulform wird in den letzten Jahren laut Text immer häufiger eingeführt?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文明确提到\'Immer mehr Schulen werden zu Gesamtschulen umgewandelt\'（越来越多的学校被改造成综合学校）。因此正确答案是C。A、B、D是传统三分制体系中的学校类型，但并非近年来的改革趋势。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Die Pandemie hatte keine Auswirkungen auf die Schulen.\", \"B. Die Digitalisierung der Schulen war bereits vor der Pandemie abgeschlossen.\", \"C. Die Pandemie hat gezeigt, dass viele Schulen technisch schlecht ausgestattet sind.\", \"D. Während der Pandemie wurden alle Schulen geschlossen.\"], \"question\": \"Was kann man aus dem Text über die Corona-Pandemie im Zusammenhang mit deutschen Schulen schließen?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文最后一句指出\'Waehrend der Corona-Pandemie wurde deutlich, dass viele Schulen in Deutschland technisch nicht ausreichend ausgestattet sind\'（新冠疫情期间明显看出许多德国学校技术设备不足）。由此可推断出选项C正确。A与原文矛盾；B错误，因为数字化尚未完成；D虽可能是事实，但文中未提及所有学校关闭，因此不能作为推断结论。\"}]'),(56,'de','Mein Tagesablauf','Hallo, ich heisse Lukas und bin siebzehn Jahre alt. Ich wohne in Muenchen und besuche die elfte Klasse eines Gymnasiums. Jeden Morgen stehe ich um halb sieben auf. Zuerst gehe ich ins Badezimmer und dusche mich. Dann fruehstuecke ich mit meiner Familie. Meine Mutter macht immer leckere Broetchen mit Marmelade und Kaese. Um Viertel vor acht verlasse ich das Haus und fahre mit dem Fahrrad zur Schule. Der Unterricht beginnt um acht Uhr. Am Vormittag habe ich meistens vier Stunden, zum Beispiel Mathe, Deutsch, Englisch und Geschichte. In der grossen Pause treffe ich meine Freunde auf dem Schulhof. Nach der Schule esse ich zu Mittag und mache eine kurze Pause. Am Nachmittag habe ich zweimal pro Woche Fusballtraining.',310,NULL,NULL,'A1','daily,life,school','2026-07-02 12:40:55',0,'[{\"word\": \"heisse\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈhaɪsə\", \"definition\": \"我叫\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"wohne\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈvoːnə\", \"definition\": \"居住\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"besuche\", \"phonetic\": \"bəˈzuːxə\", \"definition\": \"上（学）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"stehe auf\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈʃteːə aʊf\", \"definition\": \"起床\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"fruehstuecke\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈfʁyːʃtʏkə\", \"definition\": \"吃早餐\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"fahre\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈfaːʁə\", \"definition\": \"骑（车）\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"Unterricht\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈʊntɐʁɪçt\", \"definition\": \"课程\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Pause\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈpaʊzə\", \"definition\": \"休息时间\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 0, \"options\": [\"A. Lukas beschreibt seinen Tagesablauf.\", \"B. Lukas erzählt von seiner Familie.\", \"C. Lukas erklärt, wie man Fahrrad fährt.\", \"D. Lukas spricht über seine Lieblingsfächer.\"], \"question\": \"Was ist die Hauptidee des Textes?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了Lukas从早上起床到下午活动的日常安排，因此主要思想是描述他的日常作息。选项A正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Um halb sieben.\", \"B. Um acht Uhr.\", \"C. Um Viertel vor acht.\", \"D. Um Viertel nach acht.\"], \"question\": \"Wann verlässt Lukas das Haus?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到“Um Viertel vor acht verlasse ich das Haus”，因此答案是C。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Er hat jeden Tag Fußballtraining.\", \"B. Er hat nur zweimal pro Woche Fußballtraining.\", \"C. Er macht nie eine Pause nach der Schule.\", \"D. Er fährt nach der Schule mit dem Bus nach Hause.\"], \"question\": \"Was kann man über Lukas\' Nachmittage vermuten?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到“Am Nachmittag habe ich zweimal pro Woche Fusballtraining”，因此可以推断他每周只有两次足球训练，选项B正确。\"}]'),(57,'de','Wochenende in Berlin','Berlin ist die Hauptstadt Deutschlands und eine der spannendsten Staedte Europas. Letztes Wochenende bin ich mit meiner Freundin nach Berlin gefahren. Wir sind am Samstagmorgen mit dem Zug angekommen. Das Wetter war herrlich: blauer Himmel und angenehme Temperaturen. Zuerst haben wir unser Gepaeck im Hotel abgegeben und sind dann sofort losgegangen. Unser erster Halt war das Brandenburger Tor, das Wahrzeichen der Stadt. Von dort aus sind wir die Strasse Unter den Linden entlang spaziert und haben die vielen historischen Gebaeude bewundert. Am Nachmittag haben wir die Museumsinsel besucht. Der beruehmte Pergamonaltar hat uns besonders beeindruckt. Abends waren wir in einem gemuetlichen Restaurant im Stadtteil Kreuzberg und haben typisch deutsche Gerichte probiert.',310,NULL,NULL,'A1','travel,daily','2026-07-02 12:41:06',0,'[{\"word\": \"Hauptstadt\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈhaʊptˌʃtat\", \"definition\": \"首都\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Wochenende\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈvɔxn̩ˌʔɛndə\", \"definition\": \"周末\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Zug\", \"phonetic\": \"tsuːk\", \"definition\": \"火车\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Wetter\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈvɛtɐ\", \"definition\": \"天气\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Wahrzeichen\", \"phonetic\": \"ˈvaːɐ̯ˌt͡saɪ̯çn̩\", \"definition\": \"标志性建筑/地标\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"spazieren\", \"phonetic\": \"ʃpaˈt͡siːʁən\", \"definition\": \"散步\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"Restaurant\", \"phonetic\": \"ʁɛstoˈʁɑ̃ː\", \"definition\": \"餐厅\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"Gericht\", \"phonetic\": \"ɡəˈʁɪçt\", \"definition\": \"菜肴\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Berlin ist eine langweilige Stadt.\", \"B. Der Autor beschreibt einen Wochenendausflug nach Berlin.\", \"C. Der Autor arbeitet in Berlin.\", \"D. Das Wetter in Berlin war schlecht.\"], \"question\": \"Was ist die Hauptidee des Textes?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述作者上周末和朋友去柏林旅行的经历，包括交通、天气、景点和美食，因此B选项正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Am Freitagabend.\", \"B. Am Samstagmorgen.\", \"C. Am Sonntagnachmittag.\", \"D. Am Samstagabend.\"], \"question\": \"Wann sind der Autor und seine Freundin in Berlin angekommen?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到“Wir sind am Samstagmorgen mit dem Zug angekommen.”，因此B选项正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Der Autor hat Berlin schon oft besucht.\", \"B. Der Autor mochte den Pergamonaltar nicht.\", \"C. Der Autor und seine Freundin haben den Tag gut genutzt.\", \"D. Das Hotel war sehr teuer.\"], \"question\": \"Was kann man aus dem Text schließen?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：从文中可知，他们早上到达后立即出发，参观了多个景点并享用了晚餐，说明他们充分利用了时间，因此C选项正确。\"}]'),(58,'en','My Daily Routine','My name is Tom and I am a college student. Every morning, I wake up at seven o\'clock. First, I wash my face and brush my teeth. Then I have breakfast with my family. I usually eat bread with butter and drink a glass of milk. At eight o\'clock, I leave home and walk to school. The walk takes about fifteen minutes. My classes start at half past eight. In the morning, I have English and math. English is my favorite subject because the teacher is very kind and the lessons are interesting. At noon, I eat lunch in the school cafeteria with my friends. We talk about our classes and weekend plans. In the afternoon, I have science and history. Science is difficult for me, but I study hard. After school, I go to the library to do my homework. I usually stay there for about two hours. In the evening, I go back home and have dinner with my family. After dinner, I sometimes watch TV or read a book. I go to bed at eleven o\'clock. I like my daily life because it is simple and peaceful.',280,NULL,NULL,'小学','daily,life,school','2026-07-02 15:57:07',0,'[{\"word\": \"college\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkɑːlɪdʒ/\", \"definition\": \"大学\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"breakfast\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈbrekfəst/\", \"definition\": \"早餐\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"cafeteria\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkæfəˈtɪriə/\", \"definition\": \"自助餐厅；食堂\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"favorite\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈfeɪvərɪt/\", \"definition\": \"最喜欢的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"subject\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈsʌbdʒɪkt/\", \"definition\": \"科目；学科\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"difficult\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈdɪfɪkəlt/\", \"definition\": \"困难的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"library\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈlaɪbreri/\", \"definition\": \"图书馆\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"peaceful\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈpiːsfəl/\", \"definition\": \"平静的；安宁的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tom\'s favorite subject is English.\", \"B. Tom describes his daily routine as a college student.\", \"C. Tom walks to school every morning.\", \"D. Tom eats lunch with his friends.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了Tom作为大学生从早到晚的日常生活，包括起床、早餐、上课、午餐、放学后去图书馆、晚餐和睡觉等。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是其中的细节。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. He leaves home.\", \"B. He goes to school.\", \"C. He has breakfast with his family.\", \"D. He goes to the library.\"], \"question\": \"What does Tom do right after washing his face and brushing his teeth?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文提到“First, I wash my face and brush my teeth. Then I have breakfast with my family.”，所以洗完脸和刷牙后，他立刻和家人吃早餐。选项C正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Because it is easy for him.\", \"B. Because the teacher is kind and the lessons are interesting.\", \"C. Because he studies hard.\", \"D. Because it is in the morning.\"], \"question\": \"Why does Tom like English class?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：原文明确说“English is my favorite subject because the teacher is very kind and the lessons are interesting.”，因此推断他喜欢英语是因为老师友善且课程有趣。选项B正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tom\'s favorite subject is English.\", \"B. Tom describes his daily routine as a college student.\", \"C. Tom walks to school every morning.\", \"D. Tom eats lunch with his friends.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了Tom作为大学生从早到晚的日常生活，包括起床、早餐、上课、午餐、放学后去图书馆、晚餐和睡觉等。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是其中的细节。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Tom\'s favorite subject is English.\", \"B. Tom describes his daily routine as a college student.\", \"C. Tom walks to school every morning.\", \"D. Tom eats lunch with his friends.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了Tom作为大学生从早到晚的日常生活，包括起床、早餐、上课、午餐、放学后去图书馆、晚餐和睡觉等。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是其中的细节。\"}]'),(59,'en','A Weekend Trip','Last weekend, my friend Sarah and I went on a short trip to the mountains. We had been planning this trip for a long time, and we were very excited. We left early on Saturday morning and drove for about two hours. The weather was perfect: the sky was blue and the sun was warm. When we arrived, we found a nice place to park the car and started our hike. The trail was not too difficult, and there were beautiful flowers and tall trees everywhere. We could hear birds singing in the trees above us. After walking for about an hour, we stopped to rest near a small river. The water was very clear and cold. We sat on a big rock and ate the sandwiches we had brought. Sarah took many photos of the mountains and the river. She loves photography and is very good at it. In the afternoon, we walked back down to the car. We were tired but very happy. On the way home, we stopped at a small restaurant and had a delicious dinner. It was a wonderful day, and I hope we can do it again soon.',290,NULL,NULL,'小学','travel,weekend,nature','2026-07-02 15:57:19',0,'[{\"word\": \"trip\", \"phonetic\": \"/trɪp/\", \"definition\": \"旅行；短途出行\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"excited\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪkˈsaɪtɪd/\", \"definition\": \"兴奋的；激动的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"hike\", \"phonetic\": \"/haɪk/\", \"definition\": \"徒步；远足\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"trail\", \"phonetic\": \"/treɪl/\", \"definition\": \"小径；路线\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"clear\", \"phonetic\": \"/klɪr/\", \"definition\": \"清澈的；清晰的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"photography\", \"phonetic\": \"/fəˈtɑːɡrəfi/\", \"definition\": \"摄影；拍照\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"delicious\", \"phonetic\": \"/dɪˈlɪʃəs/\", \"definition\": \"美味的；可口的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"wonderful\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈwʌndərfl/\", \"definition\": \"极好的；精彩的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Sarah is good at taking photos.\", \"B. The writer and Sarah had a wonderful day trip to the mountains.\", \"C. The weather was perfect for hiking.\", \"D. They ate sandwiches near a river.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了作者和朋友Sarah上周末去山区短途旅行的经历，包括出发、徒步、休息、拍照和晚餐，整体表达了这是一次愉快的一天，因此B项最符合主旨。A、C、D都是细节，不能概括全文。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Near a small restaurant.\", \"B. At the top of the mountain.\", \"C. Near a small river.\", \"D. In the car.\"], \"question\": \"Where did the writer and Sarah stop to rest?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到“After walking for about an hour, we stopped to rest near a small river.”，因此他们休息的地方是在一条小河附近，C项正确。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Angry and disappointed.\", \"B. Tired but happy.\", \"C. Bored and sleepy.\", \"D. Worried about the drive home.\"], \"question\": \"How did the writer and Sarah probably feel at the end of the day?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到“We were tired but very happy.”，并且最后说“It was a wonderful day”，可以推断出他们虽然累但很开心，因此B项正确。A、C、D与文章内容不符。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Sarah is good at taking photos.\", \"B. The writer and Sarah had a wonderful day trip to the mountains.\", \"C. The weather was perfect for hiking.\", \"D. They ate sandwiches near a river.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了作者和朋友Sarah上周末去山区短途旅行的经历，包括出发、徒步、休息、拍照和晚餐，整体表达了这是一次愉快的一天，因此B项最符合主旨。A、C、D都是细节，不能概括全文。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Sarah is good at taking photos.\", \"B. The writer and Sarah had a wonderful day trip to the mountains.\", \"C. The weather was perfect for hiking.\", \"D. They ate sandwiches near a river.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了作者和朋友Sarah上周末去山区短途旅行的经历，包括出发、徒步、休息、拍照和晚餐，整体表达了这是一次愉快的一天，因此B项最符合主旨。A、C、D都是细节，不能概括全文。\"}]'),(60,'en','Learning a New Language','I started learning Spanish three months ago, and it has been an amazing experience. At first, I was nervous because I thought it would be too difficult. I had never learned another language before, and I did not know what to expect. My teacher, Ms. Garcia, is from Mexico. She is very patient and always encourages us to speak, even when we make mistakes. She says that making mistakes is part of learning, and I think she is right. In class, we do many different activities. Sometimes we listen to Spanish songs and try to understand the words. Other times we practice conversations in pairs. My favorite activity is when we learn about Spanish and Latin American culture. We have learned about festivals, food, and traditions from many different countries. Outside of class, I use a language app on my phone to practice vocabulary. I try to study for at least twenty minutes every day. I can already have simple conversations in Spanish, and I feel very proud. Next year, I hope to visit Spain and practice speaking with real people.',270,NULL,NULL,'小学','education,culture,study','2026-07-02 15:57:30',0,'[{\"word\": \"experience\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪkˈspɪriəns/\", \"definition\": \"经历；体验\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"nervous\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈnɜːrvəs/\", \"definition\": \"紧张的；焦虑的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"patient\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈpeɪʃnt/\", \"definition\": \"耐心的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"encourage\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪnˈkɜːrɪdʒ/\", \"definition\": \"鼓励；激励\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"mistake\", \"phonetic\": \"/mɪˈsteɪk/\", \"definition\": \"错误\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"conversation\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkɑːnvərˈseɪʃn/\", \"definition\": \"对话；交谈\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"culture\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkʌltʃər/\", \"definition\": \"文化\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"proud\", \"phonetic\": \"/praʊd/\", \"definition\": \"自豪的；骄傲的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The writer thinks learning Spanish is too difficult.\", \"B. The writer is enjoying learning Spanish and making progress.\", \"C. The writer only uses an app to learn Spanish.\", \"D. The writer wants to visit Mexico next year.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述作者学习西班牙语三个月来的积极体验和进步，因此B项最符合主旨。A项与原文‘amazing experience’矛盾；C项以偏概全，作者还用其他方式学习；D项原文是‘visit Spain’，不是Mexico。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Students should avoid making mistakes.\", \"B. Making mistakes is a sign of bad learning.\", \"C. Making mistakes is a normal part of learning.\", \"D. Only beginners make mistakes.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what does Ms. Garcia say about making mistakes?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：细节题。原文明确提到‘She says that making mistakes is part of learning’，因此C项正确。A、B、D均与原文相反。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Because the teacher is from Mexico.\", \"B. Because he/she can already have simple conversations.\", \"C. Because he/she will visit Spain next year.\", \"D. Because he/she studies for twenty minutes every day.\"], \"question\": \"Why does the writer feel proud?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：推断题。原文说‘I can already have simple conversations in Spanish, and I feel very proud’，因此自豪的原因是能够进行简单对话。A项是老师背景，C项是未来计划，D项是日常习惯，均不是直接原因。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The writer thinks learning Spanish is too difficult.\", \"B. The writer is enjoying learning Spanish and making progress.\", \"C. The writer only uses an app to learn Spanish.\", \"D. The writer wants to visit Mexico next year.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述作者学习西班牙语三个月来的积极体验和进步，因此B项最符合主旨。A项与原文‘amazing experience’矛盾；C项以偏概全，作者还用其他方式学习；D项原文是‘visit Spain’，不是Mexico。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. The writer thinks learning Spanish is too difficult.\", \"B. The writer is enjoying learning Spanish and making progress.\", \"C. The writer only uses an app to learn Spanish.\", \"D. The writer wants to visit Mexico next year.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述作者学习西班牙语三个月来的积极体验和进步，因此B项最符合主旨。A项与原文‘amazing experience’矛盾；C项以偏概全，作者还用其他方式学习；D项原文是‘visit Spain’，不是Mexico。\"}]'),(61,'en','The Rise of Remote Work','The COVID-19 pandemic fundamentally changed the way millions of people around the world work. Before 2020, working from home was relatively uncommon, typically available only to a small percentage of employees in certain industries. However, when lockdowns forced companies to close their offices, remote work became the new normal almost overnight. What started as a temporary measure has now become a permanent feature of the modern workplace. Surveys show that a majority of workers who can do their jobs remotely would like to continue doing so at least part of the time. The benefits of remote work are clear: employees save time and money by not commuting, enjoy greater flexibility in managing their schedules, and often report higher levels of job satisfaction. Companies, meanwhile, can reduce their real estate costs and hire talent from anywhere in the world, not just from their local area. However, remote work is not without its challenges. Many workers report feeling isolated and lonely when they do not see their colleagues in person. The boundary between work and personal life can become blurred, leading to longer working hours and increased stress. Additionally, not all jobs can be done remotely. Workers in retail, healthcare, manufacturing, and many other sectors must be physically present at their workplaces. This has created a new divide between those who can work from home and those who cannot. As we look to the future, the challenge for employers and policymakers will be to create a work environment that combines the flexibility of remote work with the social and collaborative benefits of in-person interaction.',410,NULL,NULL,'CET4','technology,society,work','2026-07-02 15:57:42',3,'[{\"word\": \"pandemic\", \"phonetic\": \"/pænˈdemɪk/\", \"definition\": \"大流行病\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"remote work\", \"phonetic\": \"/rɪˈmoʊt wɜːrk/\", \"definition\": \"远程工作\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun phrase\"}, {\"word\": \"commuting\", \"phonetic\": \"/kəˈmjuːtɪŋ/\", \"definition\": \"通勤\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"flexibility\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌfleksəˈbɪləti/\", \"definition\": \"灵活性\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"isolated\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd/\", \"definition\": \"孤立的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"blurred\", \"phonetic\": \"/blɜːrd/\", \"definition\": \"模糊的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"divide\", \"phonetic\": \"/dɪˈvaɪd/\", \"definition\": \"分歧；差距\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"collaborative\", \"phonetic\": \"/kəˈlæbərətɪv/\", \"definition\": \"合作的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Remote work was common before 2020.\", \"B. The pandemic made remote work widespread, and it has both benefits and challenges.\", \"C. All workers prefer to work from home full-time.\", \"D. Companies should force employees to return to the office.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了疫情使远程工作成为常态，并分析了其优点（节省时间、灵活性等）和缺点（孤独感、工作生活界限模糊等），因此B项正确。A项与原文相反；C项过于绝对；D项未提及。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Employees feel less isolated.\", \"B. Companies can reduce real estate costs.\", \"C. All jobs can be done remotely.\", \"D. Workers have longer working hours.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, which of the following is a benefit of remote work for companies?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：细节题。原文提到“Companies, meanwhile, can reduce their real estate costs”，因此B项正确。A项是员工面临的挑战；C项与原文“not all jobs can be done remotely”矛盾；D项是远程工作的缺点之一。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Everyone will work from home permanently.\", \"B. Employers will ignore the challenges of remote work.\", \"C. A balanced approach combining remote and in-person work may be developed.\", \"D. Remote work will disappear once the pandemic ends.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the future of work based on the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：推理题。文章最后一句提到“the challenge... will be to create a work environment that combines the flexibility of remote work with the social and collaborative benefits of in-person interaction”，暗示未来可能采取混合工作模式，因此C项正确。A、D项过于绝对；B项与原文强调挑战不符。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Remote work was common before 2020.\", \"B. The pandemic made remote work widespread, and it has both benefits and challenges.\", \"C. All workers prefer to work from home full-time.\", \"D. Companies should force employees to return to the office.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了疫情使远程工作成为常态，并分析了其优点（节省时间、灵活性等）和缺点（孤独感、工作生活界限模糊等），因此B项正确。A项与原文相反；C项过于绝对；D项未提及。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Remote work was common before 2020.\", \"B. The pandemic made remote work widespread, and it has both benefits and challenges.\", \"C. All workers prefer to work from home full-time.\", \"D. Companies should force employees to return to the office.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章主要讲述了疫情使远程工作成为常态，并分析了其优点（节省时间、灵活性等）和缺点（孤独感、工作生活界限模糊等），因此B项正确。A项与原文相反；C项过于绝对；D项未提及。\"}]'),(62,'en','The Problem with Single-Use Plastics','Every year, the world produces more than 400 million tons of plastic. Nearly half of this is designed to be used just once and then thrown away. These single-use plastics, which include items such as shopping bags, water bottles, straws, and food packaging, have become a major environmental crisis. The biggest problem with plastic is that it does not biodegrade. Instead, it breaks down into smaller and smaller pieces called microplastics, which can persist in the environment for hundreds of years. These tiny plastic particles have been found everywhere scientists have looked: in the deepest ocean trenches, in Arctic ice, in the air we breathe, and even in human blood. Marine animals are particularly affected by plastic pollution. Sea turtles mistake plastic bags for jellyfish, their favorite food. Seabirds feed plastic pieces to their chicks, which can cause starvation. Whales have been found dead with dozens of kilograms of plastic waste in their stomachs. Several countries have taken steps to address the problem. Many have banned single-use plastic bags, and some have gone further by restricting other disposable plastic items. However, plastic production continues to rise globally, driven largely by increasing demand in developing countries. Experts argue that solving this crisis will require a combination of approaches: reducing plastic production at the source, improving recycling systems, developing biodegradable alternatives, and changing consumer behavior. Individual actions, such as carrying reusable bags and water bottles, can help, but systemic change is essential if we are to tackle this problem effectively.',430,NULL,NULL,'CET4','environment,science,society','2026-07-02 15:57:54',3,'[{\"word\": \"plastic\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈplæstɪk/\", \"definition\": \"塑料\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"single-use\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈsɪŋɡl juːs/\", \"definition\": \"一次性的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"biodegrade\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌbaɪəʊdɪˈɡreɪd/\", \"definition\": \"生物降解\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"microplastics\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈmaɪkrəʊˌplæstɪks/\", \"definition\": \"微塑料\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"pollution\", \"phonetic\": \"/pəˈluːʃn/\", \"definition\": \"污染\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"starvation\", \"phonetic\": \"/stɑːˈveɪʃn/\", \"definition\": \"饥饿；饿死\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"disposable\", \"phonetic\": \"/dɪˈspəʊzəbl/\", \"definition\": \"可丢弃的；一次性的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}, {\"word\": \"biodegradable\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌbaɪəʊdɪˈɡreɪdəbl/\", \"definition\": \"可生物降解的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Plastic is useful but expensive to produce.\", \"B. Single-use plastics cause serious environmental problems that require multiple solutions.\", \"C. Only developing countries are responsible for plastic pollution.\", \"D. Recycling is the only way to solve the plastic crisis.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"文章主要讨论了塑料污染（尤其是一次性塑料）的严重性，并指出解决这一问题需要多种方法结合，包括减少生产、改进回收、开发替代品和改变消费者行为。选项B准确概括了主旨。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. It completely disappears within a few years.\", \"B. It breaks down into microplastics that last for hundreds of years.\", \"C. It is quickly eaten by marine animals.\", \"D. It is always recycled by waste management systems.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what happens to plastic when it is thrown away?\", \"explanation\": \"文章明确指出塑料不会生物降解，而是分解成微塑料，并在环境中存留数百年。选项B与此细节一致。\"}, {\"answer\": 2, \"options\": [\"A. Individual actions alone are enough to solve the crisis.\", \"B. The problem is too big and cannot be solved.\", \"C. Both personal efforts and large-scale changes are necessary.\", \"D. Banning plastic bags is the most effective solution.\"], \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author\'s view on solving the plastic problem?\", \"explanation\": \"文章最后提到个人行动（如携带可重复使用的袋子）有帮助，但强调系统性变革至关重要。由此可推断作者认为个人努力和系统性改变都是必要的。选项C符合这一推理。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Plastic is useful but expensive to produce.\", \"B. Single-use plastics cause serious environmental problems that require multiple solutions.\", \"C. Only developing countries are responsible for plastic pollution.\", \"D. Recycling is the only way to solve the plastic crisis.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"文章主要讨论了塑料污染（尤其是一次性塑料）的严重性，并指出解决这一问题需要多种方法结合，包括减少生产、改进回收、开发替代品和改变消费者行为。选项B准确概括了主旨。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Plastic is useful but expensive to produce.\", \"B. Single-use plastics cause serious environmental problems that require multiple solutions.\", \"C. Only developing countries are responsible for plastic pollution.\", \"D. Recycling is the only way to solve the plastic crisis.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of this passage?\", \"explanation\": \"文章主要讨论了塑料污染（尤其是一次性塑料）的严重性，并指出解决这一问题需要多种方法结合，包括减少生产、改进回收、开发替代品和改变消费者行为。选项B准确概括了主旨。\"}]'),(63,'en','The History of Coffee Culture','Coffee is one of the most popular beverages in the world, with over two billion cups consumed every day. Its journey from a humble bean in Ethiopia to a global phenomenon is a fascinating story of trade, culture, and social change. According to legend, coffee was first discovered by an Ethiopian goat herder named Kaldi in the ninth century. He noticed that his goats became unusually energetic after eating the red berries from a certain tree. Kaldi shared his discovery with a local monastery, where the monks began using the berries to stay awake during long hours of prayer. From Ethiopia, coffee spread to the Arabian Peninsula. By the fifteenth century, it was being cultivated in Yemen, and the first coffee houses appeared in cities like Mecca and Cairo. These establishments became important centers of social life, where people gathered to drink coffee, play chess, listen to music, and discuss politics. In the seventeenth century, coffee arrived in Europe and quickly became popular, despite initial suspicion from some religious authorities who called it the \'bitter invention of Satan.\' Coffee houses soon sprang up across the continent. In England, they were known as \'penny universities\' because for the price of a penny, anyone could enter and engage in intellectual discussions with scholars and writers. In the twentieth century, coffee culture underwent another transformation with the rise of international chains like Starbucks, which turned the simple act of drinking coffee into a sophisticated experience with endless variations and a new vocabulary: latte, cappuccino, macchiato, frappuccino. Today, specialty coffee shops continue to thrive, with growing consumer interest in the origin, quality, and ethical sourcing of their coffee beans.',420,NULL,NULL,'CET4','culture,history,food','2026-07-02 15:58:09',3,'[{\"word\": \"beverage\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈbevərɪdʒ/\", \"definition\": \"饮料\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"phenomenon\", \"phonetic\": \"/fəˈnɒmɪnən/\", \"definition\": \"现象\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"legend\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈledʒənd/\", \"definition\": \"传说\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"monastery\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈmɒnəstəri/\", \"definition\": \"修道院\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"cultivate\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/\", \"definition\": \"种植；培养\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"verb\"}, {\"word\": \"establishment\", \"phonetic\": \"/ɪˈstæblɪʃmənt/\", \"definition\": \"机构；场所\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"suspicion\", \"phonetic\": \"/səˈspɪʃn/\", \"definition\": \"怀疑\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"noun\"}, {\"word\": \"ethical\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˈeθɪkl/\", \"definition\": \"道德的；合乎道德的\", \"partOfSpeech\": \"adjective\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Coffee was first discovered by a goat herder in Ethiopia.\", \"B. Coffee has evolved from a simple discovery to a global cultural and social phenomenon.\", \"C. Coffee houses in Europe were called \'penny universities\'.\", \"D. Starbucks created a new coffee vocabulary.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章从咖啡的发现（埃塞俄比亚牧羊人）讲到传播（阿拉伯半岛、欧洲），再到现代咖啡文化（星巴克和精品咖啡），核心是咖啡如何从一种简单饮品发展为影响全球的文化和社会现象。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是细节。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. They were places where monks stayed awake for prayer.\", \"B. They were centers for social activities like chess, music, and political discussion.\", \"C. They were known as \'penny universities\' in England.\", \"D. They were the first places to serve Starbucks coffee.\"], \"question\": \"According to the passage, what role did coffee houses play in the fifteenth century?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中明确提到15世纪在麦加和开罗出现的咖啡馆成为重要的社交中心，人们在那里喝咖啡、下棋、听音乐和讨论政治（\'These establishments became important centers of social life...\'）。选项B正确。A是修道院的故事，C是17世纪英国的情况，D是20世纪后的发展。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Because coffee was too expensive for common people.\", \"B. Because they believed coffee was a sinful or evil invention.\", \"C. Because coffee made people too energetic.\", \"D. Because coffee houses competed with churches.\"], \"question\": \"Why might some religious authorities have initially opposed coffee in Europe?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文中提到咖啡在17世纪传入欧洲时，一些宗教权威最初持怀疑态度，称其为\'bitter invention of Satan\'（撒旦的苦涩发明）。这暗示他们认为咖啡与邪恶或罪孽有关，因此选项B正确。其他选项在文中没有依据。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Coffee was first discovered by a goat herder in Ethiopia.\", \"B. Coffee has evolved from a simple discovery to a global cultural and social phenomenon.\", \"C. Coffee houses in Europe were called \'penny universities\'.\", \"D. Starbucks created a new coffee vocabulary.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章从咖啡的发现（埃塞俄比亚牧羊人）讲到传播（阿拉伯半岛、欧洲），再到现代咖啡文化（星巴克和精品咖啡），核心是咖啡如何从一种简单饮品发展为影响全球的文化和社会现象。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是细节。\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"A. Coffee was first discovered by a goat herder in Ethiopia.\", \"B. Coffee has evolved from a simple discovery to a global cultural and social phenomenon.\", \"C. Coffee houses in Europe were called \'penny universities\'.\", \"D. Starbucks created a new coffee vocabulary.\"], \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the passage?\", \"explanation\": \"解析：文章从咖啡的发现（埃塞俄比亚牧羊人）讲到传播（阿拉伯半岛、欧洲），再到现代咖啡文化（星巴克和精品咖啡），核心是咖啡如何从一种简单饮品发展为影响全球的文化和社会现象。选项B概括了全文主旨，而A、C、D只是细节。\"}]'),(64,'en','My Daily Routine','I wake up at 7 AM every day. First, I brush my teeth and wash my face. Then I eat breakfast with my family. We usually have bread, eggs, and milk. After breakfast, I go to school by bus. It takes about 20 minutes. My classes start at 8:30. I have four classes in the morning and two in the afternoon. My favorite subject is English because I like speaking with my classmates. At noon, I eat lunch at the school cafeteria. The food is pretty good. After school, I sometimes play basketball with my friends. I go home at 5 PM. I do my homework first, then I watch TV or read books. I go to bed at 10 PM. This is my typical day.',120,NULL,NULL,'小学','daily life','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[{\"word\": \"routine\", \"phonetic\": \"/ruːˈtiːn/\", \"definition\": \"常规，惯例\"}, {\"word\": \"cafeteria\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkæfəˈtɪəriə/\", \"definition\": \"自助餐厅\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"By car\", \"By bus\", \"By bike\", \"On foot\"], \"question\": \"How does the author go to school?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I go to school by bus.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"Math\", \"English\", \"Science\", \"History\"], \"question\": \"What is the author\'s favorite subject?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'My favorite subject is English.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}]'),(65,'en','A Trip to the Zoo','Last Sunday, my parents took me to the zoo. It was a sunny day. We saw many animals there. My favorite were the pandas. They are so cute and lazy! They just sat there eating bamboo. We also watched the dolphin show. The dolphins were very smart. They could jump high and play with balls. I took many photos with my phone. At noon, we had lunch at a restaurant near the zoo. I ate a hamburger and drank orange juice. In the afternoon, we visited the aquarium. There were colorful fish and big sharks. I was a little scared of the sharks! We went home at 4 PM. I was tired but very happy. It was a wonderful day.',145,NULL,NULL,'小学','past tense','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[{\"word\": \"routine\", \"phonetic\": \"/ruːˈtiːn/\", \"definition\": \"常规，惯例\"}, {\"word\": \"cafeteria\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkæfəˈtɪəriə/\", \"definition\": \"自助餐厅\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"By car\", \"By bus\", \"By bike\", \"On foot\"], \"question\": \"How does the author go to school?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I go to school by bus.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"Math\", \"English\", \"Science\", \"History\"], \"question\": \"What is the author\'s favorite subject?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'My favorite subject is English.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}]'),(66,'en','The Internet and Education','The Internet has changed education in many ways. First, students can now access information from anywhere. They no longer need to visit physical libraries to find books. Online courses allow people to learn new skills without leaving their homes. Platforms like Coursera and Khan Academy offer free classes from top universities. However, there are also challenges. Not everyone has equal access to the Internet. This creates a digital divide between rich and poor students. Additionally, online learning requires strong self-discipline. Without a teacher watching, some students may not focus on their studies. Despite these challenges, most experts believe that technology will continue to improve education. The key is to use it wisely and ensure that all students can benefit.',168,NULL,NULL,'高中','technology','2026-07-02 18:13:43',2,'[{\"word\": \"routine\", \"phonetic\": \"/ruːˈtiːn/\", \"definition\": \"常规，惯例\"}, {\"word\": \"cafeteria\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkæfəˈtɪəriə/\", \"definition\": \"自助餐厅\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"By car\", \"By bus\", \"By bike\", \"On foot\"], \"question\": \"How does the author go to school?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I go to school by bus.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"Math\", \"English\", \"Science\", \"History\"], \"question\": \"What is the author\'s favorite subject?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'My favorite subject is English.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}]'),(67,'en','Climate Change: A Global Challenge','Climate change is one of the most pressing issues facing humanity today. Scientists agree that human activities, particularly the burning of fossil fuels, are the primary cause of global warming. The effects are already visible: melting ice caps, rising sea levels, and increasingly extreme weather events. Coastal cities face the threat of flooding, while agricultural regions experience droughts that threaten food security. Addressing climate change requires international cooperation. The Paris Agreement, signed by nearly 200 countries, aims to limit global temperature rise to well below 2 degrees Celsius. However, many experts argue that current commitments are insufficient. Individual actions, such as reducing meat consumption and using public transportation, can help. But systemic changes in energy production and industrial practices are essential to prevent the worst outcomes.',215,NULL,NULL,'CET6','environment','2026-07-02 18:13:43',4,'[{\"word\": \"routine\", \"phonetic\": \"/ruːˈtiːn/\", \"definition\": \"常规，惯例\"}, {\"word\": \"cafeteria\", \"phonetic\": \"/ˌkæfəˈtɪəriə/\", \"definition\": \"自助餐厅\"}]','[{\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"By car\", \"By bus\", \"By bike\", \"On foot\"], \"question\": \"How does the author go to school?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I go to school by bus.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"Math\", \"English\", \"Science\", \"History\"], \"question\": \"What is the author\'s favorite subject?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'My favorite subject is English.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}, {\"answer\": 1, \"options\": [\"6 AM\", \"7 AM\", \"8 AM\", \"9 AM\"], \"question\": \"What time does the author wake up?\", \"explanation\": \"The text says \'I wake up at 7 AM every day.\'\"}]'),(68,'ja','私の一日','私は毎朝七時に起きます。まず顔を洗って、歯を磨きます。それから朝ご飯を食べます。朝ご飯は普通トーストと卵と牛乳です。朝ご飯の後、バスで学校へ行きます。学校までは二十分ぐらいかかります。授業は八時半から始まります。午前中に四つ、午後に二つ授業があります。私の一番好きな科目は英語です。クラスメートと話すのが好きです。昼ご飯は学校の食堂で食べます。食べ物はとてもおいしいです。放課後、時々友達とバスケットボールをします。午後五時に家に帰ります。まず宿題をして、それからテレビを見たり本を読んだりします。十時に寝ます。これが私の普通の一日です。',95,NULL,NULL,'N5','N5 daily','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[]','[]'),(69,'ja','日本の四季','日本には四季があります。春は桜が咲いてとてもきれいです。多くの人がお花見をしに公園へ行きます。夏は暑くて湿気が多いです。夏休みに海や山へ行く人が多いです。秋は紅葉が美しい季節です。食欲の秋とも言われています。冬は寒くて、北海道などでは雪がたくさん降ります。お正月には家族が集まっておせち料理を食べます。日本の四季はそれぞれ特徴があって、どの季節も楽しめます。',112,NULL,NULL,'N4','N4 culture','2026-07-02 18:13:43',1,'[]','[]'),(70,'ja','働き方改革について','近年、日本では働き方改革が進められています。長時間労働が問題視され、残業時間の上限が設けられました。また、テレワークやフレックスタイム制度が普及し始めています。これらの改革は、従業員のワークライフバランスを改善することを目的としています。一方で、小規模企業では制度導入が難しいという課題もあります。さらに、働き方が変わることで人間関係やコミュニケーションにも変化が生じています。専門家は、テクノロジーを活用しつつ、人間同士のつながりを大切にする必要があると指摘しています。',145,NULL,NULL,'N3','N3 society','2026-07-02 18:13:43',2,'[]','[]'),(71,'ja','人工知能と社会','人工知能の急速な発展は、私たちの社会に根本的な変化をもたらしています。医療分野では、AIによる画像診断が医師の診断を補助し、早期発見の精度を高めています。一方で、自動化の進展により特定の職業が失われる可能性があります。経済学者の中には、普遍的基本所得の導入を主張する人もいます。倫理的な問題も提起されています。例えば、自動運転車が事故を起こした場合、責任は誰にあるのかという問題です。技術の発展を歓迎しつつも、その影響を慎重に検討する必要があるでしょう。',178,NULL,NULL,'N2','N2 technology','2026-07-02 18:13:43',3,'[]','[]'),(72,'ko','나의 하루','나는 매일 아침 7시에 일어납니다. 먼저 얼굴을 씻고 이를 닦습니다. 그리고 아침을 먹습니다. 아침 보통 토스트와 계란과 우유를 먹습니다. 아침 후에 버스로 학교에 갑니다. 학교까지는 20분 정도 걸립니다. 수업은 8시 반에 시작합니다. 오전에 4개, 오후에 2개 수업이 있습니다. 내가 제일 좋아하는 과목은 영어입니다. 학교에서 점심을 먹습니다. 음식은 꽤 맛있습니다. 방과 후에 가끔 친구들과 농구를 합니다. 오후 5시에 집에 갑니다. 먼저 숙제를 하고, 그 다음에 TV를 보거나 책을 읽습니다. 10시에 잠을 잡니다. 이것이 나의 보통 하루입니다.',88,NULL,NULL,'1级','TOPIK I daily','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[]','[]'),(73,'ko','한국의 사계절','한국에는 네 계절이 있습니다. 봄에는 벚꽃이 피어서 아주 아름답습니다. 많은 사람들이 벚꽃 구경을 하러 공원에 갑니다. 여름은 덥고 습기가 많습니다. 여름 방학에 바다나 산에 가는 사람들이 많습니다. 가을은 단풍이 아름다운 계절입니다. 입춘의 가을이라고도 합니다. 겨울은 춥고, 강원도 등에는 눈이 많이 옵니다. 설날에는 가족들이 모여서 떡국을 먹습니다. 한국의 사계절은 각각 특징이 있어서 어느 계절이든 즐길 수 있습니다.',105,NULL,NULL,'2级','TOPIK I culture','2026-07-02 18:13:43',1,'[]','[]'),(74,'ko','재택근무의 장단점','최근 재택근무가 많이 늘었습니다. 재택근무의 가장 큰 장점은 출퇴근 시간을 아낄 수 있다는 것입니다. 또한 집중해서 일할 수 있는 환경을 만들 수 있습니다. 하지만 단점도 있습니다. 집에서 일하면 동료들과 소통하기 어렵습니다. 또 집과 회사의 경계가 모호해져서 일과 삶의 균형을 잡기 어렵습니다. 일부 사람들은 집에서 혼자 일하는 것이 외롭다고 합니다. 앞으로 하이브리드 근무제가 더 많이 도입될 것으로 예상됩니다.',138,NULL,NULL,'3级','TOPIK II work','2026-07-02 18:13:43',2,'[]','[]'),(75,'ko','인공지능과 미래 직업','인공지능 기술의 발전은 노동 시장에 큰 변화를 가져오고 있습니다. 단순 반복 업무는 AI가 대체할 가능성이 높습니다. 그러나 창의성과 감성이 필요한 직업은 여전히 인간의 영역일 것입니다. 교육 전문가들은 미래 세대에게 코딩과 같은 기술뿐만 아니라 비판적 사고와 공감 능력을 가르쳐야 한다고 말합니다. 정부도 직업 훈련 프로그램을 확대하여 실업자들이 새로운 기술을 배울 수 있도록 지원해야 합니다. 기술 발전을 두려워하기보다는 그것을 활용하는 방법을 배우는 것이 중요합니다.',162,NULL,NULL,'4级','TOPIK II future','2026-07-02 18:13:43',3,'[]','[]'),(76,'fr','Ma journée','Je me réveille à sept heures du matin. D\'abord, je me lave le visage et je me brosse les dents. Ensuite, je prends le petit déjeuner avec ma famille. Nous mangeons habituellement du pain, des œufs et buvons du lait. Après le petit déjeuner, je vais à l\'école en bus. Ça prend environ vingt minutes. Mes cours commencent à huit heures et demie. J\'ai quatre cours le matin et deux l\'après-midi. Ma matière préférée est l\'anglais parce que j\'aime parler avec mes camarades. À midi, je déjeune à la cantine de l\'école. La nourriture est plutôt bonne. Après l\'école, je joue parfois au basket avec mes amis. Je rentre chez moi à cinq heures. Je fais d\'abord mes devoirs, puis je regarde la télé ou lis des livres. Je me couche à dix heures. Voilà ma journée typique.',142,NULL,NULL,'A1','A1 daily','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[]','[]'),(77,'fr','Les saisons en France','En France, il y a quatre saisons. Au printemps, les fleurs fleurissent et il fait de plus en plus chaud. En été, beaucoup de Français partent en vacances à la mer ou à la montagne. L\'automne est la saison des vendanges. Les feuilles des arbres deviennent jaunes et rouges. En hiver, il fait froid et il peut neiger dans le nord. Noël est une fête très importante en France. Les familles se réunissent autour d\'un grand repas. Chaque saison en France a son charme particulier.',128,NULL,NULL,'A2','A2 culture','2026-07-02 18:13:43',1,'[]','[]'),(78,'fr','Le télétravail','Depuis la pandémie, le télétravail s\'est développé rapidement en France. De nombreuses entreprises ont adopté le travail hybride. Les employés peuvent travailler deux ou trois jours par semaine chez eux. Cette organisation présente plusieurs avantages. D\'abord, on gagne du temps en transport. Ensuite, on peut mieux concilier vie professionnelle et vie familiale. Cependant, le télétravail pose aussi des problèmes. Certains employés se sentent isolés. D\'autres ont du mal à séparer travail et vie personnelle. Les entreprises doivent donc accompagner leurs salariés dans cette transition.',155,NULL,NULL,'B1','B1 work','2026-07-02 18:13:43',2,'[]','[]'),(79,'fr','L\'intelligence artificielle et l\'éducation','L\'intelligence artificielle transforme profondément le secteur de l\'éducation. Les plateformes d\'apprentissage adaptatif personnalisent les parcours selon le niveau de chaque élève. Les chatbots peuvent répondre aux questions des étudiants à toute heure. Cependant, cette révolution soulève des questions importantes. Comment protéger les données personnelles des élèves ? L\'IA peut-elle vraiment remplacer l\'accompagnement humain ? Les experts s\'accordent sur un point : la technologie doit rester un outil au service de l\'enseignant, non un substitut. L\'enjeu est de former les jeunes à utiliser ces outils de manière critique et responsable.',178,NULL,NULL,'B2','B2 technology','2026-07-02 18:13:43',3,'[]','[]'),(80,'de','Mein Tagesablauf','Ich wache jeden Tag um sieben Uhr auf. Zuerst wasche ich mein Gesicht und putze mir die Zähne. Dann frühstücke ich mit meiner Familie. Wir essen normalerweise Brot, Eier und trinken Milch. Nach dem Frühstück fahre ich mit dem Bus zur Schule. Es dauert etwa zwanzig Minuten. Der Unterricht beginnt um halb neun. Ich habe vier Stunden am Morgen und zwei am Nachmittag. Mein Lieblingsfach ist Englisch, weil ich gerne mit meinen Klassenkameraden spreche. Um zwölf esse ich in der Mensa. Das Essen ist ziemlich gut. Nach der Schule spiele ich manchmal Basketball mit meinen Freunden. Ich gehe um fünf Uhr nach Hause. Zuerst mache ich meine Hausaufgaben, dann sehe ich fern oder lese Bücher. Ich gehe um zehn Uhr ins Bett. Das ist mein typischer Tag.',158,NULL,NULL,'A1','A1 daily','2026-07-02 18:13:43',0,'[]','[]'),(81,'de','Die Jahreszeiten in Deutschland','In Deutschland gibt es vier Jahreszeiten. Im Frühling blühen die Blumen und es wird immer wärmer. Im Sommer fahren viele Deutsche in den Urlaub an die See oder in die Berge. Der Herbst ist die Zeit der Weinlese. Die Blätter der Bäume werden gelb und rot. Im Winter ist es kalt und im Norden kann es schneien. Weihnachten ist ein sehr wichtiges Fest in Deutschland. Die Familien kommen zu einem großen Essen zusammen. Jede Jahreszeit in Deutschland hat ihren eigenen Reiz.',142,NULL,NULL,'A2','A2 culture','2026-07-02 18:13:43',1,'[]','[]'),(82,'de','Homeoffice in Deutschland','Seit der Pandemie hat sich Homeoffice in Deutschland schnell entwickelt. Viele Unternehmen haben hybrid Arbeit eingeführt. Die Mitarbeiter können zwei oder drei Tage pro Woche von zu Hause arbeiten. Diese Organisation hat mehrere Vorteile. Zuerst spart man Zeit im Transport. Dann kann man Berufs- und Familienleben besser vereinbaren. Allerdings gibt es auch Probleme. Manche Mitarbeiter fühlen sich isoliert. Andere haben Schwierigkeiten, Arbeit und Privatleben zu trennen. Die Unternehmen müssen ihre Mitarbeiter bei diesem Übergang begleiten.',168,NULL,NULL,'B1','B1 work','2026-07-02 18:13:43',2,'[]','[]'),(83,'de','Künstliche Intelligenz und Bildung','Künstliche Intelligenz verändert den Bildungssektor grundlegend. Adaptive Lernplattformen personalisieren die Lernwege nach dem Niveau jedes Schülers. Chatbots können zu jeder Zeit Fragen der Studenten beantworten. Diese Revolution wirft jedoch wichtige Fragen auf. Wie schützt man die persönlichen Daten der Schüler? Kann KI den menschlichen Begleiter wirklich ersetzen? Die Experten sind sich in einem Punkt einig: Die Technologie muss ein Werkzeug im Dienst des Lehrers bleiben, kein Ersatz. Die Herausforderung besteht darin, junge Menschen zu befähigen, diese Werkzeuge kritisch und verantwortungsvoll zu nutzen.',185,NULL,NULL,'B2','B2 technology','2026-07-02 18:13:43',3,'[]','[]');
